      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Corrected architecture from user:\n- Helix agent lives on Dell 630 (Proxmox VM)\n- OKF server also on Dell 630 (separate Proxmox VM)\n- Main PC is the target machine where actual coding occurs\n- ALL scanning is remote over local network (Dell 630 → Main PC)\n\nKey requirements:\n1. Add config section [helix.project_scanner] + [[helix.projects]] array in config.toml.\n2. Per-project settings: name, target_machine (\"main-pc\"), remote_path, protocol (smb | ssh | http | local), include/exclude globs, max_depth.\n3. Per-PC settings block for hosts, auth methods, credentials placeholders.\n4. Core scanner capable of local walks today + remote access (start with mounted SMB share or stub for SSH/file-server).\n5. Rich output metadata: source_machine=\"main-pc\", scanned_from=\"dell630\", timestamp, file counts, etc.\n6. Reuse/extend existing scan_directory + generate_mermaid_project_map from task 167.\n7. Expose as tool: scan_projects (and scan_remote_project).\n8. Output must be directly usable for OKF knowledge entries (content_type \"file-tree\" or \"project-map\").\n\nRemote access strategy options:\n- SMB/CIFS share mounted on Dell 630 pointing to Main PC\n- SSH from Dell 630 to Main PC\n- Small dedicated file-server or agent running on Main PC that Helix calls\n\nMermaid priority: Generate Mermaid file-tree / project-map diagrams (not Markmap for now, unless user confirms otherwise).",
      "testStrategy": "Configure a project in config pointing at a network path (or local mount for dev). Run scanner from Dell 630 context and verify output contains correct source_machine/scanned_from metadata + usable tree for Mermaid generation. Test include/exclude and depth limits.",
