      "description": "No OKF server implementation exists anywhere reachable; build the minimal reference server per PROTOCOL.md v1.",
      "details": "2026-10-04 REFRAME: no standalone server exists or is needed yet — Helix already contains the server half (see task 207 finding). This task is now: complete/wire the IN-Helix OKF server — enablement path ([helix.okf] enabled), reconcile mounted routes with the v1 protocol from 207, verify Helix can fetch from itself, systemd/deploy notes for the Ubuntu box. Only build a separate standalone server if John asks for it. FINDING (2026-10-04): searched ~/workspace (client code only), the Drive helix folder (schema + sample manifest + deploy notes only), and the micro-tech GitHub org (no okf repo) — there is no OKF server implementation anywhere reachable. 'It doesn't work' because it was never built. DECISION FOR JOHN BEFORE STARTING: repo home (suggest new micro-tech/okf-server) and deploy target (the Ubuntu box on the R630). Do not start until he confirms. BUILD (Rust + axum, matches his stack): serve a bundle directory on disk. GET /okf/health -> {\"status\":\"ok\"}; GET /okf/manifest.json and /okf/bundles/{id}/manifest.json (ETag support); GET /okf/knowledge/{kid}; POST /okf/traces (append JSONL); POST /okf/bundles/{bundle}/concepts (append concept, update manifest). Optional Bearer auth via env var; bind 127.0.0.1 default, LAN bind explicit. Ship with a systemd unit example and the diagnostic curl commands from the 2026-10-04 runbook.",
      "id": 208,
      "results": "In-Helix OKF server completed (no standalone built -- reframed per 2026-10-04 finding). New v1 routes: GET /okf/manifest.json, GET /okf/bundles/{id}/manifest.json, GET /okf/knowledge/{kid}, POST /okf/traces (202, JSONL append to [helix.okf] trace_file), POST /okf/bundles/{bundle}/concepts (201, inserts knowledge entry + persists index). Librarian retains current_manifest; ETag/304 on manifest GETs; /okf/health returns status:ok. New require_okf_write_token middleware accepts web token OR okf auth_token Bearer, fail-open when neither configured. config.toml [helix.okf] documents v1 + trace_file; deploy runbook in PROTOCOL.md. Tests: 3 self-fetch integration tests green (Helix fetches from itself); full lib suite 263 passed, 0 failed; zero new warnings.",
