      "description": "The 2026-10-05 mega-batch (tasks 187-208) added 8 new dead-code/unused warnings to cargo check --lib (9 baseline lines -> 17). None break the build, but two need judgment calls (rule_layer never read; web_server config fields never read). Clean them so the tree is warning-free again.",
      "details": "FILED BY QUARTERMASTER 2026-10-05 ~05:00 EDT. METHOD: stashed the mega-batch working tree, ran cargo check --lib --message-format=short (9 unique warning lines), unstashed, re-ran (17 lines). Diff = 8 new lines, all in mega-batch code. RULED OUT: pre-existing warnings untouched (unix_socket x3, okf/fetcher resp, okf/registry Path import, tools/mod other, runtime_trace i, cpu/mod target (line shifted 916->1274 only), build-script std::env). NEW WARNINGS: (1) src/acp/agent.rs:22 unused import crate::agents::simple_planner::SimplePlanner -- the module docs explicitly say SimplePlanner is NOT used; delete the import. (2) src/agents/runtime_loop.rs:13 field rule_layer: RuleLayer never read -- constructor stores it, no method reads self.rule_layer. FUNCTIONAL QUESTION, not just lint: was the rule layer supposed to validate/retry steps in the loop (tasks 157/158 Tool Supervisor v2)? Wire it or allow(dead_code) with a comment; do not blindly underscore. (3)-(7) src/io/web_server/mod.rs -- Config.helix, Config.heartbeat, HelixConfig.name, OllamaConfig.url/model, WebConfig.port, HeartbeatConfig.interval_seconds never read. These are #[derive(Deserialize)] config-schema structs from the UI rework (193-198); check WebConfig.port especially (where does the server get its bind port? if from elsewhere, flag the inconsistency). (8) src/tools/project_scanner.rs:326 walk_ssh_directory (cfg(not(feature=ssh)) fallback) flagged never-used -- CHECK ARTIFACT, not real dead code: it IS called by test_ssh_walk_fallback_when_feature_disabled (line 669, cfg(test)); cargo check --lib does not compile test code. Verify with cargo check --lib --tests that the warning vanishes, then cfg_attr(not(test), allow(dead_code)) with comment. OBSERVATION (not a warning, for the repair plan): src/tools/project_scanner.rs:57-63 hardcodes \"youruser\" and None key_path with TODOs to load from scanner_cfg.machines[target_machine] -- the real SSH path cannot authenticate until pending task 171 lands. Not a new failure; noted so the plan accounts for it.",
