      "results": "DONE 2026-10-05 ~06:15 EDT by Ranger 1. All 8 warnings eliminated; cargo check --lib --bins shows only pre-existing baseline lines. 210.1: deleted dead SimplePlanner import (acp/agent.rs); walk_ssh_directory silenced via cfg_attr(not(test), allow(dead_code)) with comment (only caller is the cfg(test) fallback test). 210.2: #[allow(dead_code)] + why-comments on web_server parse-schema mirror fields; bind port confirmed to arrive via the start_web_server() argument from main.rs (schema field redundant, documented). 210.3: rule_layer WIRED per plan - RuntimeLoop::run() validates every ToolCall via RuleLayer::validate before execution; rejections land in the transcript (recoverable), consume step budget (no infinite spin), consecutive-call counter resets on non-tool decisions; ACP allowlist fixed to [system_status] (empty set would have rejected its own grounding call). 210.4: full lib suite 265 passed (263 + 2 new runtime_loop tests), 0 failed, 4 ignored. CHALLENGES: (a) walk_ssh warning does NOT vanish under cargo check --lib --tests (lib target still warns); cfg_attr approach verified correct instead. (b) tests/integration_harness.rs and other tests/*.rs are PRE-EXISTING broken (old bot:: crate name, 18 E0433 on base commit) - blocks cargo check --tests; NOT fixed (out of scope), noted in CHANGELOG. DEVIATION: added 2 unit tests for the new wiring (wiring an untested safety check without tests would be malpractice)."
