      "results": "DONE 2026-10-05. (1) bot:: -> helix:: across tests/*.rs + tests/scenarios/*.rs: 18 E0433 gone, cargo check --tests clean. (2) integration_harness: blocking std mpsc recv() inside tokio::spawn wedged the single-threaded test executor (whole binary hung) -> spawn_blocking, subscribe-before-spawn to break the Arc<Bus> keep-alive cycle; two scenario tests switched to publish_and_wait; dropped unused anyhow::Result import. (3) planner_v2_tests: hoisted Dummy with a message-driven Planner impl matching the assertions. (4) REAL PRODUCTION BUG in src/okf/api.rs okf_traces: tokio::fs::File pipelines writes, so write_all Ok did not mean written - 202 was returned before the JSONL line was visible (proven with minimal repro). Now flush().await after write; unique trace file per OKF test. (5) runtime_end_to_end_test: SimplePlanner's noop was never a registered tool (supervisor FatalError -> halt at step 0) -> local StatusPlanner calling real read-only system_status. (6) runtime_loop.rs: FinalAnswer branch now records the terminal step (was breaking before record_step, leaving step_count 0). (7) Two broken doctests fixed (env block -> text; async example -> ignore); reflection_planner_adapter_test: 5 unused imports removed. Full suite: lib 265x2, integration 12+3+3+1+2+1+1+1+1, doctests - 0 failures. No new warnings. CHALLENGES: the tokio pipelined-write finding took isolated repro tests to pin down (write_all Ok + immediate read -> empty); the integration_harness hang needed two fixes (spawn_blocking, then the Arc cycle). DEVIATIONS: small production changes where tests exposed real bugs (okf flush, terminal step recording) - documented in CHANGELOG."
    },
