      "dependencies": [],
      "description": "6 lib tests fail at b7f76b3 (baseline e0fa353: 265 passed / 0 failed / 4 ignored; now 259 passed / 6 failed / 4 ignored). Root cause: John's commit abc747f (merged via PR #10 master->PreRelese) enabled [mcp] enabled=true and the google server in the repo config.toml; the tests assume the worktree config leaves MCP disabled.",
      "details": "Failing tests: (1) mcp_client::tests::disabled_by_default_from_worktree_config - assert!(!is_enabled()) at src/mcp_client/mod.rs:165 fails because config now enables MCP. (2) mcp_client::tests::try_execute_returns_none_for_mcp_names_when_disabled - try_execute(mcp__google__gmail_search) returns Some(spawn error) instead of None; it tried to spawn /home/cobble/.local/bin/google-mcp which does not exist in this sandbox. (3-6) a2a::a2a_handler::tests::message_send_creates_and_completes_task, cancel_terminal_task_is_noop, acp::agent::tests::run_prompt_produces_final_answer, run_prompt_unknown_session_still_runs - panic at src/mcp_client/mod.rs:103: 'can call blocking only when running on the multi-threaded runtime' via bridge()/block_in_place, because the tests now take the MCP-enabled path on a current-thread runtime. REPAIR DIRECTION: make the tests hermetic - point them at an isolated test config (or env-gated fixture) instead of the worktree config.toml. Do NOT just re-disable [mcp] in config.toml: John enabled it deliberately for his deployment (google-mcp binary at /home/cobble/.local/bin/google-mcp on the R630). Check how is_enabled() locates config.toml and inject a test override. RULED OUT: build is green (exit 0), no new warnings (11 unique, all pre-existing; 5 fixed by the same merges), no disk issues (this was a clean rerun after /tmp was freed; grok-cli fully green). Full failure output: ~/workspace/goals/nightly-quartermaster-run/hidden_files/qm-20261008-bot-test.log\n\nSURVEYOR 1 REPAIR PLAN (2026-10-08, verified by backtrace — planning only, no code touched): GOAL: make the lib unit tests hermetic w.r.t. the worktree config.toml's [mcp] section. Zero production behavior change; John's enabled [mcp] + google server entry in config.toml stays exactly as he committed it (abc747f). VERIFIED ROOT CAUSE: #[tokio::test] defaults to current_thread flavor (backtrace shows current_thread::Core driving the test fn — NOT multi-thread). mcp_client::bridge() does Handle::try_current() -> Ok -> block_in_place, which panics on current-thread runtimes. With [mcp] enabled, the 4 agent-loop tests reach bridge() via describe_tools_for_prompt -> tool_definitions -> mcp_client::tool_definitions. Production unaffected (tokio::main is multi-thread; no current_thread runtime anywhere in src/). ALSO SPOTTED: 2 false-green tests pass only because the spawn of the absent google-mcp binary fails; on John's R630 (binary present) they'd attempt real MCP handshakes in unit tests.\n\nPHASES: (1) hermetic config plumbing in src/mcp_client/mod.rs only (HELIX_MCP_CONFIG_PATH env override + #[cfg(test)] default when CONFIG_PATH unset); (2) rewrite the 2 worktree-coupled tests; (3) the 4 a2a/acp tests need NO edits (Phase 1b makes is_enabled() false); (4) full lib suite green with John's enabled config.toml untouched + CHANGELOG entry, commit on PreRelese, push on John's cards. REJECTED: re-disabling [mcp] (John's deliberate deployment choice), multi_thread test flavor (would attempt real spawns on equipped machines), .cargo/config [env] (would neuter local dev runs), reworking bridge() (production change, zero production benefit — deferred). RISKS: bridge() still panics on current-thread runtimes (future prod hazard — follow-up candidate); no hermetic enabled-path spawn coverage (fake-stdio fixture — follow-up). (Reconstructed 2026-10-08 after the working-tree filing was lost; see nightly-quartermaster-run/hidden_files/run-2026-10-08.md.)",
