      "dependencies": [],
      "description": "New LLM tool so any backend (the 'commander' John chats with) can spin up a sub-agent on a chosen backend. This is the missing piece John hit on 2026-10-08: 'run a sub agent to plan out a bot app in rust' got clarifying questions because no such tool exists in src/tools/mod.rs.",
      "details": "New file src/tools/subagent_tool.rs (or add to system_tools.rs — Ranger's call, keep it consistent with the module layout). Tool name: spawn_subagent. Params: task (string, required) — the marching orders; backend (string, optional) — one of local_ollama | lan_ollama | gemini | grok | auto (default auto); role_hint (string, optional) — planner | builder | reviewer | ui | free text. Dispatch design: reuse the A2A task-creation pattern (a2a/tasks.rs TaskStore::create) and run the prompt on the shared agent runtime loop (acp/agent.rs run_prompt) bound to the selected backend, exactly like a2a_handler.rs handle_message_send does with tokio::spawn. When backend=auto (or omitted), build a RoutingContext from the task text and call router::route() for the pick. Return to the commander: task id, chosen backend, and the sub-agent's final message (block with a configurable timeout; on timeout return partial status + task id so the commander can poll). Guardrails (non-negotiable): max spawn depth (a sub-agent may NOT spawn sub-agents beyond depth 1 — pass depth in and enforce, prevents infinite delegation loops); API-backend calls increment the spend counter used by task 217. Wire into execute() match in src/tools/mod.rs AND add the JSON schema to static_tool_definitions() (the file's own docs demand they stay in sync; there is a test asserting definitions are stable). Branch: PreRelese. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\n[Ranger 1 2026-10-08] Built. Deviations from plan: (1) did NOT reuse A2A TaskStore/run_prompt — no global TaskStore exists and run_prompt's AcpPlanner can only call system_status, useless for real sub-agent work. The runner drives the backend's native chat-with-tools loop (Ollama) or single-shot prompt (Gemini) instead. (2) On timeout the worker is cancelled; no poll-after-timeout registry (follow-up candidate). (3) Grok returns 'not implemented' — no client exists in the codebase. All 8 subagent + 4 spend unit tests pass; 6 pre-existing suite failures (a2a/acp/mcp_client) confirmed unrelated via clean-tree run. Zero new warnings.",
