      "details": "In src/cron/registry.rs extend Routine with: agent_role (string, e.g. 'quartermaster' or free text), task (string, the prompt), backend (string, same enum as spawn_subagent incl. auto), all serde-defaulted so existing routines keep working. spawn_scheduler: include the payload in the routine_run bus message. CPU/heartbeat job-pump: handle routine_run WITH payload by dispatching through the same path as spawn_subagent (task 214's dispatch fn — refactor it into a shared helper both the tool and the cron handler call). Routine without payload (legacy) keeps today's behavior. Seed one example routine in the default registry: twice-daily inbox check ('every 12h', agent_role quartermaster-style mail check) mirroring John's existing mail agent. Expose payload fields in the WS/HTTP routine API so the web UI can create/edit them (Sapper 1 may take the UI half — see task 219). Branch: PreRelese. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\n[Ranger 1 2026-10-08] Built. Routine{agent_role,task,backend} serde-defaulted (old files load fine); payload published in routine_run bus message; CPU handle_routine_run dispatches payload jobs via dispatch_spawn (shared helper with the tool), logs + nightly_report the result; legacy id-based routines unchanged; seeded disabled twice-daily mail_check example; WS routines_list exposes payload fields (create/edit UI is Sapper 1's 219). 16 cron tests pass.",
