      "description": "Define exactly how spawn picks a backend: explicit param wins, else the complexity router decides, with health-aware fallback and a daily API spend cap that stops paid escalation and asks John.",
      "details": "Document the policy in src/router/docs.rs (or a new POLICY.md in src/router/): ladder local_ollama -> lan_ollama -> gemini -> grok. Rules: (1) explicit backend param on spawn_subagent always wins (this is also John's manual UI override path via user_override); (2) backend=auto builds a RoutingContext and calls router::route() — note route() currently never selects LanOllama, decide its role (overflow/embeddings box at 192.168.1.149 vs general) and wire it in or document why not; (3) health-aware fallback: RoutingContext already carries health — if the chosen backend is unhealthy, walk down the ladder; (4) cost caps: [router] daily_api_cap_usd (default 5.00); every Gemini/Grok call decrements; at cap, paid backends are refused with a message routed to John (web UI notice + log) and the job falls back to local or waits. Persist spend state across restarts (beliefs.json or a small state file, not just memory). Keep John's hardware truth in the doc: desktop 3060 = fast interactive, R630 = patient batch (Helix host itself), ollama box = embeddings/overflow, APIs = heavy hitters that cost per token. Branch: PreRelese. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\n[Ranger 1 2026-10-08] Built. Ladder documented in router/docs.rs: local (desktop 3060, fast) -> lan (ollama box, overflow; route() never selects it directly — explicit pick or fallback only) -> gemini (paid, spend-gated) -> grok (not implemented). Explicit backend wins, else complexity router decides. [router] daily_api_cap_usd parsed in main.rs (default $5.00) -> spend::set_daily_api_cap_usd; refusal message is John-facing and returns via the commander report. dispatch_spawn probes the chosen rung (/api/tags, 60s cache) and falls back down the ladder, noting every fallback in the report. main.rs endpoint mapping now sends 'desktop'-named entries to local.",
