      "details": "Sapper 1: (1) In chat, when the commander calls spawn_subagent, show a delegation card/inline status ('delegated to sub-agent on gemini… working… done') instead of silence, and render the sub-agent's returned summary distinctly. (2) Routines UI: list cron routines with their payload (agent_role/task/backend/schedule/enabled) and allow create/edit/enable/disable — backend API from task 216. Keep the existing backend picker untouched. Coordinate with Ranger 1 on the WS message shapes. Branch: PreRelese (Sapper's usual fix-* branch workflow per repo convention).\n\n[Sapper 1 2026-10-08] Built on PreRelese, single-file index.html only (no new assets).\n219.1 chat delegation: handleMessage now handles {type:\"tool_call\"}; spawn_subagent calls render a delegation card in #chat-messages with backend badge (local/LAN/Gemini/Grok/auto), role_hint, task (400ch cap), and the sub-agent's result_preview in a distinct \"sub-agent report\" block. Other tools stay silent (restraint). Contract verified against src/io/ollama/mod.rs tool_call publish. FINDING for Ranger 1: the Gemini backend (src/io/llm_gemini/mod.rs) has NO tool-calling loop and publishes no tool_call messages — the commander pattern cannot delegate there until function calling is added to the Gemini path. UI renders whatever arrives; nothing invented.\n219.2 routines: UI now sends {type:\"routines_list\"} on every WS (re)connect (it never did before — the section could never populate). Rows show agent_role/backend/task payload from task 216. New ＋New/Edit modal with fields name, schedule, agent_role, task, backend select, enabled, delete. Save sends the documented shapes {type:\"routine_create\"|\"routine_update\", name,schedule,agent_role,task,backend,enabled} and {type:\"routine_delete\", id} — these need backend support (no Rust touched per boundary); the UI waits 5s for {type:\"routine_status\"|\"routine_saved\", id, ok} and shows an explicit inline error on timeout instead of failing silently. When Ranger 1 adds the 3 messages, the UI lights up with zero changes. NOTE: backend sends schedule as human display text (\"Every day at 2:00 AM\") which does not round-trip to canonical form — edit field starts empty with the current value as placeholder hint; suggest backend echo raw schedule or accept display form.\nTests: node DOM-stub harness (/tmp/sapper219_test.js), 20/20 pass — delegation card content/badge/role/report, non-spawn silence, empty-args degrade, routines payload render, editor validation, create shape, timeout honesty, confirm-close+refresh, toggle isolation. node --check clean. Follow-up simplification: once backend routine CRUD lands, drop the 5s-timeout path to a straight confirm.\n",
