      "details": "Ranger 1, PreRelese branch. Sapper 1's UI contract (from task 219 report, verified):\n- UI sends {type:\"routine_create\"|\"routine_update\", name, schedule, agent_role, task, backend, enabled}\n- UI sends {type:\"routine_delete\", id}\n- UI waits 5s for {type:\"routine_status\"|\"routine_saved\", id, ok} and shows inline error on timeout/no-confirm.\nBuild:\n220.1 registry: add RoutineRegistry::add (generates unique id, validates schedule via parse_schedule, refreshes next_run, persists), ::update (patch fields by id, re-validate schedule, persist), ::remove (by id, persist). Unit tests for each incl. bad-schedule rejection and id uniqueness.\n220.2 WS handlers in src/io/web_server/mod.rs next to routine_toggle: \"routine_create\" validates schedule with parse_schedule — on bad input reply {type:\"routine_saved\", id:\"\", ok:false, msg} ; on success reply {type:\"routine_saved\", id, ok:true}. \"routine_update\" same shape (unknown id -> ok:false). \"routine_delete\" replies {type:\"routine_status\", id, ok}. All three persist via registry.save().\n220.3 schedule round-trip: routines_list currently serves human display text (\"Every day at 2:00 AM\") which the editor cannot parse back. Add \"schedule_raw\" (canonical \"daily HH:MM\" / \"every <n>s|m|h|d\") to each routine in the list reply; keep \"schedule\" display text for backward compat (task 197 contract). routine_create/update accept the canonical form in \"schedule\".\nKeep existing tests green; CHANGELOG entry.\n\n[Ranger 1 2026-10-08] Built. Deviation: WS arms have no socket-level test (no WS client harness in suite) — thin wrappers over tested registry methods; live UI drill stays in 218. Full suite: 286 pass, 6 pre-existing failures unchanged.",
      "testStrategy": "cargo test cron:: registry add/update/remove incl. bad schedule rejection; WS-level: drive the three new message types through the existing web_server test harness (see the routines test at web_server/mod.rs:~1522) asserting confirm shapes; routines_list asserts schedule_raw parses via parse_schedule.",
