        214
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Ranger 1, PreRelese branch. Mirror the Ollama backend's tool loop (src/io/ollama/mod.rs — the tool_call publish contract Sapper verified against):\n221.1 Declare the shared tool set (from the same tool definitions 214 wired, INCLUDING spawn_subagent) as Gemini functionDeclarations on the generateContent request.\n221.2 Implement the call/response loop: send functionResponse parts back, iterate until the model returns text (cap iterations, same guardrails style as the Ollama loop).\n221.3 Publish {type:\"tool_call\"} messages on the bus for every tool invocation, same shape the Ollama path publishes, so the UI delegation cards work on Gemini too.\n221.4 Commander prompt: confirm the 215 commander block reaches the Gemini path (it may already via shared prompt assembly — verify, don't assume).\nDo NOT require John's real API key in the sandbox. Mock the HTTP layer for the headless drill. Any live-key verification is John's step (task 218 territory).\nKeep existing tests green; CHANGELOG entry. Document deviations from this brief in the task details.\n\n[Ranger 1 2026-10-08] Built. Deliberate choices: (1) every generateContent round calls note_api_call so the 217 spend cap sees real usage; (2) the shared reqwest error diagnosis was extracted to map_reqwest_err and reused by the old single-shot path; (3) call_gemini_direct (spawn runner) and call_gemini_sync stay single-shot on purpose. Test note: mockito matches FIFO not LIFO, so the drill uses one mock with an atomic hit counter for sequenced responses. Full suite: 289 pass, 6 pre-existing failures unchanged.",
      "testStrategy": "Headless drill with mocked Gemini HTTP: feed a prompt that must delegate, assert the Gemini path emits a spawn_subagent function call AND publishes a {type:\"tool_call\"} bus message. Unit tests for functionDeclarations serialization. cargo test green overall.",
