      "details": "Implemented: POST /ops/update (auth-gated) spawns a detached self-update job running git pull && cargo build --release && cargo run --bin installer; GET /ops/update/status polls {running, log_tail}. Detachment: systemd-run --scope (cgroup escape so the installer's systemctl stop helix can't SIGTERM the updater) with setsid fallback in safe mode (pull+build only, installer skipped with manual-finish instructions). cargo PATH export included. Job files: logs/web-update.{sh,log,pid} next to the chat log (task-188 path rule). UI: Update button + live log panel + status line, polls every 3s, resumes after reconnect. NOTE: installer needs root — headless sudo requires a NOPASSWD rule or the log shows sudo's complaint.",
      "testStrategy": "cargo check clean (no new warnings); 27/27 io::web_server lib tests pass incl. 6 new ops unit tests (script content full/safe modes, quoting, tail_chars, process_alive, read_pid) + 3 HTTP contract tests (401 without token on all 3 endpoints; status polling live/stale pid; restart failure returns structured JSON). JS syntax validated with node --check. Live dry-run of the full update left to John on the R630 (would rebuild + restart the live service).",
