    {
      "id": 230,
      "title": "Backend: sub-agent registry + agent_status feed for the web UI",
      "description": "Track live sub-agents and per-backend activity on the server, and push an agent_status snapshot over the existing WS broadcast so the left panel can show sub-agent entries with working/idle indicators.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [],
      "details": "GOAL: the web UI left panel must list live sub-agents (icon + short description + working indicator) and show a working/idle indicator on every backend entry. Today there is NO registry: dispatch_spawn (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs:342) generates task_id at line 368, blocks to completion, and returns; the only UI signal is the tool_call bus event, which both the Gemini path (src/io/llm_gemini/mod.rs:445) and the Ollama path publish AFTER execution completes — so the UI can never show a live sub-agent. Fix that with a registry plus push events, following the existing task-219 tool_call contract.\n\nSUBTASKS:\n230.1 SubagentRegistry: new file src/agents/subagent_registry.rs (or extend subagent_tool.rs if cleaner). Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, SubagentRecord>>> shared via OnceLock or web_server state. Record: { id (subagent-<uuid>, same as dispatch_spawn line 368), backend (e.g. 'desktop'), role_hint (short description; fall back to '(any)'), task_summary (task text truncated to 120 chars), status: Working|Done|Failed|TimedOut, started_at_ms, finished_at_ms }. Hook dispatch_spawn: register immediately after task_id is created; update status in each of the three completion arms (Ok / Err / timeout). Prune: keep all Working entries plus the last 10 finished (bounded memory). Process-global is fine — cron/heartbeat/one-shot subagents are stateless, spawn_subagent is the only spawn path.\n\n230.2 Lifecycle bus events: publish {\"type\":\"subagent_event\",\"event\":\"spawned|finished\",\"subagent\":{...record...}} to bus address \"web_interface\" at register and at finish (same publish contract as the tool_call event at llm_gemini/mod.rs:445). Add \"subagent_event\" to the bridge forward-as-is list in src/io/web_server/mod.rs (~line 806) so it fans out to WS clients.\n\n230.3 agent_status snapshot: build fn in web_server/mod.rs producing {\"type\":\"agent_status\",\"backends\":[{\"id\",\"activity\":\"idle|working\"}],\"subagents\":[{...records...}]}. Send it on every WS connect right after the existing backends send (~line 677), and re-broadcast via state.msg_tx on every registry change (spawn/finish). Client re-renders from the snapshot — no incremental-sync state, payload is tiny (a few backends + a few subagents).\n\n230.4 Backend activity tracking: web_server state gets Arc<Mutex<HashSet<(String backend_id, u64 correlation_id)>>> in-flight set. Insert at the chat_request publish site (mod.rs ~line 1116, where `llm` and `correlation_id` are both in scope). In the bridge thread, extend the forwarded ollama_response / llm_output JSON with correlation_id when present in the inner bus data, and remove the matching entry. activity = working iff any in-flight entry for that backend. Add a 5-minute TTL sweep task for entries whose backend never answered (stuck 'working' otherwise). If the response path turns out not to carry correlation_id, fallback: per-backend boolean set on chat_request, cleared on the next response from that backend — document which you shipped.\n\nDECISION POINTS FOR JOHN (do not guess, surface in the PR/report): (a) sub-agent list is global across all chats — ok, or scope to the current WS session? (b) keep last 10 finished entries greyed in the panel, or remove rows the moment they finish? (c) should a sub-agent row be clickable (e.g. show its full report), or display-only? Recommended: global, keep-10, display-only — but John's call.\n\nKeep the existing auth model: these are read-only status broadcasts on the existing broadcast channel, same as backends/tool_call today. No new HTTP endpoints needed.\n\nRESULTS (Ranger 1, 2026-10-10, branch web-ops-buttons):\n- 230.1 DONE: new src/agents/subagent_registry.rs (wired into src/agents/mod.rs). Process-global Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, SubagentRecord>>> via OnceLock. Record {id, backend, role_hint (''(any)'' fallback), task_summary (120-char truncation), status Working|Done|Failed|TimedOut, started_at_ms, finished_at_ms}. dispatch_spawn registers immediately after task_id creation and finishes in all three completion arms (Done/Failed/TimedOut); the HELIX_SUBAGENT_TEST_STUB path also runs the lifecycle with a generated id. Prune keeps all Working + last 10 finished. Locks are dropped before bus publish / status-listener notify (deadlock audit: listener re-locks for its snapshot).\n- 230.2 DONE: register/finish publish {\"type\":\"subagent_event\",\"event\":\"spawned|finished\",\"subagent\":{...}} to bus address \"web_interface\" (task-219 tool_call contract). Published via a new process-global bus handle (crate::bus::set_global_bus/global_bus, installed in main.rs); silent no-op when absent. \"subagent_event\" added to the bridge forward-as-is list in web_server.\n- 230.3 DONE: agent_status_snapshot()/build_agent_status() produce {\"type\":\"agent_status\",\"backends\":[{id,activity}],\"subagents\":[{...}]}; sent on every WS connect right after the backends message; re-broadcast via state.msg_tx on every registry change through a set_status_listener hook installed once at server startup (NOT per-connection). Clients re-render wholesale.\n- 230.4 DONE: AppState.inflight: Arc<Mutex<HashMap<u64 correlation_id, (String backend_id, u64 sent_at_ms)>>> — deviation from the spec'd HashSet<(String,u64)>: the map carries sent_at so the 5-min TTL sweep can reap without a second structure. Inserted at the chat_request publish site (backend_id derived from bus_dest, ms-collision bump for key uniqueness); snapshot re-broadcast on insert. Bridge (extracted to testable bridge_out_message()) extends forwarded llm_output/ollama_response JSON with correlation_id when present and retires the matching entry, then re-broadcasts agent_status. Supporting fix: main.rs CPU forwarder now preserves correlation_id from llm_response into llm_output (it was dropped). 60s-interval TTL sweep task reaps entries older than 5 min + re-broadcasts. Fallback (per-backend boolean) NOT needed — correlation_id path verified working.\n- 230.5 DONE: 9 new tests, all green. Registry: lifecycle, prune (3 working + 14 finished -> 3 + 10), 8-thread concurrent register/finish no-deadlock, JSON shape. subagent_tool: stubbed dispatch_spawn emits spawned->finished on a bus subscriber in order (recv_timeout for the router-thread handoff). web_server: snapshot shape (activity flags + subagent row), subagent_event forwarded as-is, bridge retires in-flight on response and flips activity working->idle, unmatched response forwards without retiring.\n- cargo check --lib --tests: clean (only pre-existing warnings: build.rs, unix_socket.rs, unix_socket_test.rs). Full lib suite: 314 passed, 6 failed — the 6 are pre-existing task-213 failures (a2a x2, acp::agent x2, mcp_client x2), verified identical on the pristine tree via git stash. (One full run showed 2 transient chat_history failures that did not reproduce on re-run; they pass in isolation — parallel-test flake, unrelated.)\n- DECISION POINTS FOR JOHN (from spec, still open): (a) sub-agent list global across chats (shipped) vs per-session; (b) keep last 10 finished greyed (shipped) vs remove on finish; (c) rows display-only (shipped) vs clickable for full report. Recommended: global, keep-10, display-only.\n- INCIDENT: mid-task `git checkout .zed/task_list.json` wiped working-tree tasks 230-232 (they were never committed). 230 restored verbatim from the agent's context (only statuses advanced); 231/232 reconstructed from the parent brief + memory notes and marked RECONSTRUCTED — parent must verify 231/232 details against Surveyor 1's originals.",
      "testStrategy": "cargo check clean (apart from pre-existing warnings). cargo test --lib tools::subagent_tool — new unit tests: register->finish lifecycle, prune keeps 10 finished, concurrent register/finish doesn't deadlock. cargo test --lib io::web_server — new tests: agent_status snapshot shape (backends[].activity present, subagents[] present), subagent_event passes the bridge forward list, in-flight insert/remove flips activity. Integration: spawn a subagent via the HELIX_SUBAGENT_TEST_STUB path and assert spawned+finished events hit a bus subscriber in order.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "230.1",
          "title": "SubagentRegistry struct + dispatch_spawn hooks + prune policy",
          "status": "done",
          "dependencies": []
        },
        {
          "id": "230.2",
          "title": "subagent_event bus publish + bridge forward list",
          "status": "done",
          "dependencies": [
            "230.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "230.3",
          "title": "agent_status snapshot build + send on connect + re-broadcast on change",
          "status": "done",
          "dependencies": [
            "230.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "230.4",
          "title": "Backend in-flight activity tracking (correlation_id) + TTL sweep",
          "status": "done",
          "dependencies": [
            "230.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "230.5",
          "title": "Unit + web_server tests for registry, events, snapshot",
          "status": "done",
          "dependencies": [
            "230.2",
            "230.4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 231,
      "title": "Web UI: sub-agent rows + working/idle indicators in the left panel",
      "description": "Render live sub-agents in the web UI left panel (icon + short description + working indicator) and show a working/idle indicator on every backend/agent entry, driven by the task-230 agent_status feed.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [
        230
      ],
      "details": "RECONSTRUCTED 2026-10-10 after accidental task_list.json checkout wiped working-tree entries 230-232; verify against Surveyor 1's original. Sapper 1. Consume the task-230 backend contract: `agent_status` snapshot {type, backends[{id, activity: idle|working}], subagents[{id, backend, role_hint, task_summary, status, started_at_ms, finished_at_ms}]} sent on WS connect and re-broadcast on every change, plus `subagent_event` {event: spawned|finished, subagent} messages forwarded as-is over the WS bridge. Left panel: add a sub-agents section listing each record with the Artificer 1 icon (John picked subagent-icon-v2.png, ~/workspace/your_files/), role_hint/task_summary text, and a working indicator while status == working. Every backend/agent entry gets a working/idle dot driven by backends[].activity. Re-render from each agent_status snapshot wholesale (no incremental-sync state). Keep the existing scroll fix (min-height: 0) intact.\n\nSAPPER 1 RESULTS (2026-10-10 ~22:05 EDT):\n- Built in src/io/web_server/static/index.html (working tree, branch web-ops-buttons):\n  - \"Sub-agents\" section under #backend-list in the left sidebar (hidden until records exist).\n  - Each row: Artificer 1's subagent-icon-v2.png inlined as base64 data URI under BACKEND_ICONS.subagent (verified byte-identical to ~/workspace/your_files/subagent-icon-v2.png), role_hint name, task_summary truncated via CSS ellipsis (full text in title tooltip), pulsing cyan dot while status==working, greyed row when done/failed/timed_out.\n  - Backend .status-dot spans now driven by agent_status: pulsing cyan = working, solid green = idle, muted grey = unknown (pre-snapshot).\n  - WS handlers: handleAgentStatus(msg) re-renders wholesale from each agent_status snapshot (backend activity map + subagent list); handleSubagentEvent(msg) upserts the delta record and re-renders. refreshBackendDots() repaints dots without rebuilding buttons (preserves backend selection).\n  - Inline WS branches refactored into named handleAgentStatus/handleSubagentEvent for testability.\n- Constraints honored: Rust backend untouched (read-only reference); scroll fix (min-height: 0 on #chat-panel and #chat-messages) intact; ops-button code untouched.\n- Verification: node --check clean; functional harness (/tmp/agent-test.js with minimal DOM stub) exercised the exact task-230 contract payloads — backends render neutral dots pre-status; agent_status paints working/idle dots and renders 2 rows (working pulsing, done greyed); subagent_event finish upserts in place; spawn adds a row; empty snapshot clears rows and hides the section. One real bug found by the harness (empty snapshot left stale hidden rows) and fixed. ALL AGENT-STATUS UI TESTS PASSED.\n- Deliverable (file cannot be pushed via CLI): ~/workspace/your_files/web-subagents-index.html (159,271 bytes) — complete updated index.html for John's GitHub web upload to PreRelese.\n- Follow-up improvement (per Sapper spec): rows are display-only; a click could open the sub-agent's full report in the detail panel (John's call — currently shipped as display-only per his confirmed decision).\n",
      "testStrategy": "RECONSTRUCTED — verify. node --check on the edited script; manual UI drill against a live Helix: spawn a sub-agent via chat, watch the row appear with working indicator and flip on finish; backend dot flips working->idle across a chat round-trip.",
