    {
      "id": 233,
      "title": "agent.md persona files: editable + self-authoring personas for Helix and sub-agents",
      "description": "Give Helix and its sub-agents file-based personas. <runtime_dir>/agent.md is Helix's persona block; <runtime_dir>/agents/<role>.md are per-role sub-agent personas. Persona + job description compose as separate system-prompt blocks (persona first). Missing file falls back to today's hardcoded behavior byte-identically. Agents can draft their own persona on first run and revise it later, behind an opt-in gate with draft-for-review approval. Each role file also declares its allowed-tools allowlist (frontmatter), enforced at spawn: least-privilege containment per role.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "GOAL: John's locked decisions — (1) persona + job description are SEPARATE blocks, persona first; the existing hardcoded COMMANDER_SYSTEM_PROMPT becomes the job block. (2) Self-authoring twice: (a) NOW — agent drafts its own persona file initially; (b) LATER — agent revises its own file on goof/mistake/better-idea (self-correction loop). (3) NEW: each sub-agent persona file declares its allowed-tools allowlist — least-privilege containment per role (a web-search sub-agent must not write files even if prompt-injected).\n\nRECON (verified in code, not vibes):\n- Prompt assembly today: COMMANDER_SYSTEM_PROMPT const (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs:37) is the job block. commander_system_message() (line 53) wraps it as {\"role\":\"system\"} and is used ONLY by the Ollama chat path (src/io/ollama/mod.rs:587). The Gemini path references the const DIRECTLY at src/io/llm_gemini/mod.rs:195 and :390 — bypassing commander_system_message(). Ranger MUST unify all three sites through one composed function or the Gemini path silently keeps the old prompt.\n- Sub-agents get NO system prompt today: run_subagent() (subagent_tool.rs:508) sends a single user-role message. role_prefix() (line 178) has hardcoded blurbs for planner/builder/reviewer/ui, else \"Role: X.\" passthrough. Toolset today: tool_definitions_excluding(&[\"spawn_subagent\"]) — everything else allowed. There is no per-role file today.\n- File resolution precedent: runtime_dir() (src/main.rs:94) = parent of the loaded config.toml (task 188). system_manifest.md uses candidates [rt_dir.join(name), CWD name], first-exists-wins (main.rs:274-284). agent.md follows this EXACT pattern.\n- Config gate precedent: [helix.commander] enabled parsed ad-hoc from toml::Value in main.rs:200-209. New knob [helix.persona] self_author follows the same pattern (default false — opt-in).\n\nSUBTASKS:\n233.1 New module src/persona.rs: resolve_persona_dir() (runtime dir via OnceLock set from main.rs, same ENDPOINTS pattern as subagent_tool.rs:88-92); load_persona(role: Option<&str>) -> Option<Persona> where Persona { body: String (frontmatter stripped), tools: Option<Vec<String>> } — None role reads <rt>/agent.md, Some(role) reads <rt>/agents/<role>.md with role sanitized to [a-z0-9-_] lowercase, path traversal (.., /) rejected to fallback; composed_system_prompt(role) -> Option<String> returning \"<persona>\\n\\n---\\n\\n<job>\" when a persona file exists, or just \"<job>\" when missing (byte-identical to today). Commander-disabled gate preserved (None stays None).\n233.2 Unify injection sites: refactor commander_system_message() to call composed_system_prompt(None); replace BOTH direct COMMANDER_SYSTEM_PROMPT refs in llm_gemini/mod.rs (lines ~195, ~390) with the composed text. Extract the sub-agent job text from run_subagent()'s format string into a SUBAGENT_JOB_PROMPT const (the \"Complete the task with your tools...\" portion); run_subagent() composes persona (role file, role_prefix() kept as fallback when no file) + job. Ollama sub-agents: prepend a REAL system message (today they get user-only — fix this). Gemini sub-agents (call_gemini_direct): add system_instruction with the composed text.\n233.3 Document agent.md format (no shipped default file — missing = fallback keeps behavior identical). Format doc lives in the task results: freeform markdown persona + optional YAML frontmatter (see 233.7).\n233.4 Initial self-authoring (behind [helix.persona] self_author=true, default false): when agent.md is missing at startup, Helix drafts its own via a meta-prompt (\"You are Helix... write your agent.md persona: who you are, how you work, tone...\") and writes it to <rt>/agent.md.pending (NOT live). Sub-agents: when agents/<role>.md is missing at spawn, the COMMANDER drafts the role persona pre-spawn (one LLM call on the commander's backend, cheaper than inside the worker) to agents/<role>.md.pending. Announce pending drafts in chat.\n233.5 Revision loop: triggers — (a) sub-agent task ends Failed/TimedOut, the worker may append a lesson to its role file; (b) Helix itself may revise agent.md after a user correction (\"no, do it like X\"). Guards (all mandatory): 4KB size cap per file; keep last 3 revisions as agent.md.bak.1..3 (rotation, append-only history); max 1 revision per file per hour (rate limiter in the persona module, in-memory is fine — restarts reset it, acceptable); revision prompt must include the current file content and a strict \"surgical edit, keep what works\" instruction. Runaway guard: if 3 consecutive revisions happen within the hour window (should be impossible via the limiter — defense in depth), disable self-authoring and alert John.\n233.6 Approval: ALL self-authored writes land as .pending files, NEVER live directly. Provide apply_pending_persona(path) + discard_pending_persona(path) and wire them to a chat command (\"approve persona\" / \"discard persona\") so John can review in chat. Web UI editor for agent.md is OUT OF SCOPE — note as follow-up for Sapper 1 (reuse the task-213 config-editor modal pattern).\n233.7 Tool allowlist per role (John's containment requirement): role files declare allowed tools in YAML frontmatter:\n    ---\n    tools: [web_search, gmail_read]\n    ---\n    # Searcher\n    ...persona prose...\n  The persona module strips frontmatter before injecting the persona block (the model never sees the allowlist as prose). dispatch_spawn/run_subagent() filters tool definitions to (allowlist ∩ (all tools minus spawn_subagent)) — spawn_subagent can NEVER be re-added by an allowlist (depth guard stays absolute). Migration safety: file WITH frontmatter tools -> enforced; file WITHOUT tools key -> current behavior (all tools); NO file -> current behavior. Unknown tool names in the list: log warn + ignore; if zero known names remain, fall back to current behavior + loud warning (a typo must not brick the role). DECISION FOR JOHN (flagged, not guessed): long-term default-deny (roles without a file get a minimal safe set)? RECOMMENDATION: not yet — default-deny would break existing commander flows that rely on full-tool sub-agents; revisit after the allowlist has mileage. Ship default-allow with per-role opt-in containment.\n\nACCEPTANCE: persona file present -> system prompt contains persona block then job block in order, on Ollama AND Gemini paths; file missing -> prompts byte-identical to pre-change; role traversal attempts fall back safely; self-author round-trip writes .pending not live; revision limiter refuses 2nd write within the hour; .bak rotation keeps exactly 3; allowlist filters spawn toolset (verified: searcher role cannot see file-write tools); spawn_subagent never appears in a sub-agent toolset even if listed.",
      "testStrategy": "cargo check clean (apart from pre-existing warnings). New unit tests in src/persona.rs: load_present_returns_content, frontmatter_stripped_from_injected_persona, load_missing_returns_none, compose_order_persona_then_job, compose_missing_file_is_byte_identical_to_const, role_sanitization_rejects_traversal (\"../../etc\", \"a/b\", \"..\"), revision_rate_limiter_refuses_second_write_within_hour, bak_rotation_keeps_exactly_3. Allowlist tests: parse_tools_frontmatter, unknown_tool_names_warned_and_ignored, empty_after_filter_falls_back_to_full_set, spawn_subagent_never_allowlisted, no_file_means_unfiltered_toolset. Filtering test: build tool definitions for a stub role with tools:[web_search] and assert no write/file/shell tools present. Integration: with HELIX_PERSONA_TEST_STUB=1 (stub the draft LLM call), missing agent.md -> .pending written -> apply_pending_persona() -> reload picks it up; commander_system_message() returns None when HELIX_COMMANDER_ENABLED=0 (existing test still passes). Run cargo test --lib persona tools::subagent_tool — all green. Manual: none required (file behavior is fully unit-testable).",
