      "review_type": "gap",
      "results": "236.1 GEMINI: parse_gemini_usage extracts usageMetadata at both response sites (call_gemini_tools per-round loop + call_gemini used by call_gemini_direct); metered via note_api_usage, estimate fallback when metadata absent. Removed the duplicate note_api_call in call_gemini_direct (would double-count). 236.2 OLLAMA: parse_ollama_usage extracts prompt_eval_count/eval_count in call_ollama_tools; backend attributed by URL (127.0.0.1/localhost/::1 -> LocalOllama, else LanOllama); $0 cost, tokens recorded. 236.3 SPEND REWORK: SpendState now per-day/per-backend {usd, prompt_tokens, completion_tokens, calls}; legacy flat-f64 state files auto-migrate. Pricing: $0.10/$0.40 per 1M in/out (Flash tier, approximate — update per model). 236.4 EXPOSURE: auth-gated GET /ops/usage returns usage_summary_today(). CAP DECISION (for John): default is now WARN + log on cap exceed (was block); [router] cap_block_on_exceed=true restores block. Recommend keeping warn (a hard block orphans in-flight sub-agent work). TESTS: 10 spend tests green (metered pricing, fallback, warn/block modes, parsers, migration, persistence); llm_gemini 6/6, web_server 31/31, full lib 346 passed / 6 failed = pre-existing task-213 baseline, no regressions."
    },
    {
      "id": 237,
      "title": "P1: Cache tool definitions instead of rebuilding per spawn",
      "description": "Cache the built MCP-tool JSON schema list in a OnceLock; rebuild only when the tool registry changes.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "GOAL: remove per-spawn schema-rebuild overhead from the commander hot path (John's #1 priority area: performance).\n\nDetails: the full tool JSON schema list is currently reconstructed from scratch on every dispatch_spawn, but schemas don't change at runtime. Build once into a process-global OnceLock (same pattern as the subagent registry in src/agents/subagent_registry.rs); add an explicit invalidate hook called only when the tool registry changes. Touch points: src/tools/mod.rs (tool_definitions / tool_definitions_excluding), src/persona.rs (subagent_tool_definitions consumes them).\n\nAcceptance: second and subsequent spawns reuse the cached definitions (verify with a unit test asserting the builder runs once across N spawns); registry-change path invalidates correctly.",
      "testStrategy": "cargo check clean. New unit test: build-once assertion across multiple spawns; invalidation test triggers rebuild after a simulated registry change. Full lib suite: no new failures.",
      "subtasks": [],
      "review_type": "perf",
      "results": "P1 tool-definition cache shipped. tool_definitions() now serves from a process-global RwLock<Option<Value>> (fast-path clone); build_tool_definitions() runs once on miss. The real cost was mcp_client::tool_definitions() blocking on the async manager per spawn. invalidate_tool_definitions() wired into okf::set_global_librarian and the OKF bundle-reload path (replaces TODO). 3 new tests green (build-once x10, invalidation rebuild, excluding reuses cache). Full lib: no new failures — chat_history flake confirmed pre-existing (fails on pristine tree)."
    },
