      "details": "FILED BY SURVEYOR 1, 2026-10-13. SYSADMIN-01 support-mail system, phase 1.\n\nEXTERNAL DEPENDENCY (John, NOT a build task): mail-mcp binary must land at /home/cobble/.local/bin/mail-mcp on the R630 with mailbox credentials in its environment (mail-mcp is one-mailbox-per-process, env-var config). Everything in tasks 255-260 builds and unit-tests WITHOUT the binary (mocks/stubs); only task 260's live drill needs it installed.\n\n1. config.toml: add a commented [[mcp.servers]] template block right after the google entry (config.toml:106-108):\n   [[mcp.servers]]\n   name = \"mail\"   # tools appear as mcp__mail__<tool>\n   command = \"/home/cobble/.local/bin/mail-mcp\"\n   # [mcp.servers.env]\n   # MAIL_MCP_... = \"...\"   # exact var names per mail-mcp README; do NOT commit real values\n   Mirror the pattern in src/config/mcp.rs doc comment.\n2. docs/mcp.md: add a \"mail-mcp (support@ watcher)\" section: install pointer, env vars, tool namespace, one-mailbox-per-process note (a second mailbox = second server entry).\n3. Graceful degradation: verify what mcp_client/manager.rs does today when a configured command does not exist (it should log a clear warning and simply not advertise that server's tools, never crash boot). If it crashes or spams, fix it. Add/extend a unit test with a bogus command path.\n4. Tool-name verification procedure (runs on the R630 once John installs): list tools via the manager and record the exact mcp__mail__* tool names (expected: some form of check_inbox/list_messages + send_message, but mail-mcp's surface is NOT known in this sandbox — do not hardcode guesses; the poll loop in task 256 must resolve names at runtime or from config). Document the confirmed names in docs/mcp.md.",
