      "priority": "high",
      "details": "FILED BY SURVEYOR 1, 2026-10-13. SYSADMIN-01 support-mail system, phase 3.\n\n1. Pending draft store: support_drafts/ JSON files (id, in_reply_to message id, to, subject, body, playbook_refs, created_at, status=pending|approved|sent|discarded). Drafting NEVER sends — stage only.\n2. Chat commands in the web UI command handler, mirroring /persona (task 233, src/io/web_server/mod.rs:2030+):\n   /support drafts            - list pending drafts\n   /support approve <id>      - John reviews text, marks approved (does NOT send)\n   /support send <id>         - sends ONLY an approved draft via mcp__mail__* send tool\n   /support discard <id>      - drop a draft\n   Approve and send are deliberately two steps; a single \"approve+send\" shortcut is NOT wanted (John's standing rule: irreversible actions need his explicit go-ahead, and sending email is irreversible).\n3. HARD INVARIANT (no-auto-send): no code path may invoke the mail send tool except the explicit /support send <id> handler acting on an approved draft. Encode as a test: attempt to send an unapproved/nonexistent draft id -> refused with a clear error; grep the codebase for send-tool call sites in review.\n4. Drafts record which playbook entries informed them (task 258) and link the original message id, so John sees provenance when reviewing.\n5. Auto-send categories: DEFAULT IS NONE. If John later blesses categories, that is a separate task with its own approval — this task must not build any auto-send path.",
      "testStrategy": "Unit tests: draft lifecycle (stage->approve->send->sent, stage->discard). Invariant tests: send with unapproved id refused; send with unknown id refused; no test or code path sends without approval. Chat-command handler tests for /support subcommands.",
