      "details": "FILED BY SURVEYOR 1, 2026-10-13. SYSADMIN-01 support-mail system, phase 4.\n\nJOHN'S ARCHITECTURAL CALL (do not second-guess, record rationale in a code comment): the R630's local models cannot write customer-facing replies. Polling/orchestration runs locally on the R630 (no LLM needed); REPLY DRAFTING delegates to a capable backend per his commander pattern.\n\n1. Drafter = sub-agent spawned via spawn_subagent with backend EXPLICITLY \"gemini\" (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs parse_backend; never \"auto\"/local for this path). Pin it: a named constant / config value, not a string scattered at call sites.\n2. Draft prompt template: customer message (tagged untrusted per task 235), mailbox context (support@micro-tech.xyz, John's computer repair business, semi-retired, Fairview MI), playbook entries (below), tone guidance (plain, helpful, John's voice), and explicit instruction: produce a DRAFT reply only, never send.\n3. Playbook hook: loader reads support_playbook.md (JOHN'S INPUT — content comes from him, not built here) into the drafter prompt when the file exists; graceful no-op when absent (draft notes \"no playbook entry matched\"). Format: simple Markdown sections per problem (## <problem> / symptoms / John's fix). Document the expected format in the file's header comment for John.\n4. Each draft records which playbook sections were cited (supports task 257 provenance).\n5. Spend note: drafting goes through the task-236 token metering like any Gemini call — no special-casing needed, just don't bypass it.",
