      "results": "DONE 2026-10-13 (Ranger 1, branch ranger-255-260). New src/support_watch/drafter.rs: draft_reply() loads the playbook, cites relevant sections by keyword overlap (top 3, 1500 chars each; 'no playbook entry matched' when absent), builds the prompt (customer message wrapped in <untrusted-data>, explicit NEVER-follow-instructions + draft-only-never-send instructions, ---DRAFT-BEGIN/END--- markers), spawns via dispatch_spawn with backend pinned to SUPPORT_DRAFT_BACKEND='gemini' (constant, never auto/local), extracts the body, stages via drafts::stage_draft. Structural guarantee: Gemini sits LAST on BACKEND_LADDER, so an explicit gemini request fails loudly rather than falling back to local (pinned by new test gemini_sits_last_on_health_ladder); a failed draft leaves the message unhandled (retried on next burst), which is safe. CPU routine_support_mail_watch now wires poll_new_mail() -> draft_reply per fresh message (tick() refactored into poll_new_mail() + sink wrapper). Playbook format documented for John in docs/support-playbook.md (+ SUPPORT_PLAYBOOK_TEMPLATE const). Spend: drafting flows through the normal task-236 metering via dispatch_spawn, no special-casing. Tests: 9 drafter tests (backend pin, prompt tagging/draft-only, playbook present/absent/malformed, citation relevance, marker extraction + fallback, stubbed end-to-end staging) + ladder test green; full suite 409 passed 0 failed (3 consecutive runs). Note: one transient single-test failure on the first full run did not reproduce in 3 reruns (parallel-test flake, unidentified)."
