      "id": 262,
      "title": "installer bin: include_str! of never-tracked .grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md (fresh-clone build break)",
      "description": "src/bin/installer.rs:267 does include_str!(\"../../.grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md\"), but the file has never been committed to the repo (path moved by b3fe19b, 2026-06-16; git ls-files shows 0 .grok files). Any fresh clone fails to build the installer bin. Currently masked in the main sandbox checkout only by an untracked local copy of the file.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [
        261
      ],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "FILED BY QUARTERMASTER, 2026-10-14 nightly run (spotted during the task-261 failure investigation).\n\nRULED OUT:\n- Not caused by the PR #20/21/22 merges: the include_str! line predates them (in PreRelese since June 2026).\n- No build script generates the file (build.rs only touches .grok/diagrams).\n- No CI regenerates it (repo has no .github/workflows at all).\n- Not gitignored into existence elsewhere: the main-checkout copy is untracked-but-present; a fresh worktree lacks it and fails.\n\nSUGGESTED START: pick one — (a) commit the manifest into the repo at a stable path (src/ or docs/), (b) replace the compile-time include_str! with a runtime read + graceful fallback, or (c) drop the embed if the installer no longer needs the default manifest. John's call if the manifest content is load-bearing for the installer. Do this after/independently of task 261; both must be green for a fresh-clone `cargo build` to pass.\n\nSURVEYOR 1 PLAN (2026-10-14). CRITICAL FINDING: the local .grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md is a 7-line STUB that reads 'LOCAL COMPILE STUB — NOT FOR SHIPMENT ... Do not commit this stub — .grok/ is gitignored for exactly this reason' (.gitignore line 20 ignores .grok/ wholesale). So option (a) 'commit the manifest' is OFF the table without John's explicit content blessing: the stub must never ship, and the real manifest lives only on his dev machine. RECOMMENDED: replace compile-time include_str! (src/bin/installer.rs:267) with a runtime read + baked-in minimal fallback. Concrete: const FALLBACK_MANIFEST: &str = \"# System Manifest\\n\\n(default placeholder baked at compile time; replace with the real .grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md at install time)\\n\"; fn load_default_manifest(source_dir: &Path) -> String { try source_dir.join(\".grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md\") via fs::read_to_string, fall back to FALLBACK_MANIFEST }. Call-site: deploy_tracked_file(\"system_manifest.md\", &source_dir, &load_default_manifest(&source_dir), &primary_runtime_dir) — note the existing deploy_tracked_file already prefers a runtime on-disk file and only uses the embedded default as fallback, so this change fits the installer's existing design. John's decision needed on ONE thing: whether the manifest content is load-bearing for the verify step (installer.rs:255-271 says it writes the embedded default and verify checks they match) — if he wants the real manifest shipped, he must supply its content; otherwise the placeholder fallback stands and can be refined later. ALTERNATIVE CONSIDERED (rejected): generate the file in build.rs — rejected because there is no in-repo source content to generate it from; build.rs cannot conjure the gitignored real manifest. Second alternative (rejected): commit a tracked fallback copy and keep include_str! — rejected because it ships stub content into /etc/helix and the runtime dir on every install, contradicting the stub's explicit 'NOT FOR SHIPMENT' warning.\n\nUPDATE BY QUARTERMASTER 2026-10-18 ~04:35 EDT: STILL BROKEN on PreRelese tip 92d7ae3, and the shape changed. PR #25 (master->PreRelese) included 7696e59 'rename config.toml' -> example.config.toml (live config.toml is now untracked+gitignored), so installer.rs:266 include_str!(\"../../config.toml\") now fails with 'No such file or directory' for a SECOND reason - the file is gone by name, not just absent. installer.rs:267 include_str!(\"../../.grok/docs/system_manifest_root.md\") still fails (file never tracked). Full log: ~/workspace/goals/nightly-quartermaster-run/hidden_files/qm-20261018-bot-build.log. The 262.4 decision for John stands and is now sharper: point the installer at example.config.toml (and decide whether embedding the template is acceptable), and decide the manifest question (262.4: is the manifest content load-bearing for the installer verify step?).",
      "testStrategy": "Fresh git worktree (no untracked .grok present) -> cargo check --lib --bins: exit 0. Verify the installer bin compiles and its DEFAULT_MANIFEST embeds the intended content.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "262.1",
          "status": "pending",
          "title": "src/bin/installer.rs: replace include_str! (line 267) with runtime load_default_manifest() + FALLBACK_MANIFEST constant"
        },
        {
          "id": "262.2",
          "status": "pending",
          "title": "Fresh worktree check (no .grok present): cargo check --lib --bins -> exit 0 (fresh-clone simulation)"
        },
        {
          "id": "262.3",
          "status": "pending",
          "title": "Confirm installer behavior: runtime .grok file preferred when present, baked-in fallback otherwise; verify step still matches"
        },
        {
          "id": "262.4",
          "status": "pending",
          "title": "Ask John: is manifest content load-bearing for the installer verify step? If yes, he supplies the real content"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 263,
      "title": "Fix flaky chat_history test: clear_empties_history bypasses test_env_lock and races the other chat_history tests",
      "description": "cargo test --lib on fix-bin-support-watch @ 12b8cbd failed once with chat_history::tests::corrupt_lines_dont_break_reload asserting 0 turns instead of 2, then passed on an immediate re-run with zero code changes. Scheduling-dependent flake: clear_empties_history does not use with_clean_history, so it takes no test_env_lock and mutates the shared process-global history (record_turn/clear) while other chat_history tests run in parallel.",
      "status": "done",
      "results": "Done 2026-11-05. 263.1 repro fired repeatedly on unfixed code (corrupt_lines_dont_break_reload panicked at src/chat_history.rs:324:13, 2/8 runs). 263.2 wrapped clear_empties_history in with_clean_history. 263.3 audit: only default-suite test touching shared chat_history globals without the lock; stray logs/chat_history.jsonl (x/y turns) was test pollution, removed. 263.4 verify: chat_history 10x 0 failures, full lib 10x 0 failures (605/0/4), single-threaded 605/0/4. (263.4 leave-uncommitted clause superseded by the build order: branch pushed, John merges.)",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "FILED BY QUARTERMASTER, 2026-10-16 nightly run. Production code NOT implicated (lib suite is green on re-run; the flake is test isolation only), but a flaky test reds the line intermittently and must not be ignored.\n\nFAILURE OUTPUT (full log: ~/workspace/goals/nightly-quartermaster-run/hidden_files/qm-20261016-bot-full.log):\n  thread 'chat_history::tests::corrupt_lines_dont_break_reload' panicked at src/chat_history.rs:312:13:\n  assertion `left == right` failed\n    left: 0\n   right: 2\n  failures:\n      chat_history::tests::corrupt_lines_dont_break_reload\n  test result: FAILED. 422 passed; 1 failed; 4 ignored\n\nRE-RUN (same tree, same command, minutes later; log qm-20261016-bot-testlib-rerun.log): test result: ok. 423 passed; 0 failed; 4 ignored.\n\nMECHANISM (verified in src/chat_history.rs): with_clean_history() takes crate::tools::subagent_tool::test_env_lock() (a process-global Mutex) and points HELIX_CHAT_HISTORY_FILE at a temp file. All chat_history tests use it EXCEPT clear_empties_history (src/chat_history.rs:265), which calls record_turn(\"x\", \"y\") + clear() with no lock. A clear() landing between another test's load_from_disk() and its recent_turns() assert produces exactly the observed 0-turns failure. Note with_clean_history's temp file name is pid-only (helix-chat-history-test-{pid}.jsonl), so it is shared by every chat_history test in the process — the lock is the only isolation.\n\nRULED OUT:\n- Not a code change: the tree is byte-identical to the 2026-10-15 green run (fix-bin-support-watch @ 12b8cbd, no new commits anywhere).\n- Not the 261/262 build breaks: the lib crate compiles and the lib suite runs; 261/262 block only the bins + non-lib test targets.\n- Not stale worktree state: the temp file is removed at the start/end of every with_clean_history call; the failure is a live interleaving, not leftover data.\n\nSUGGESTED START: wrap clear_empties_history's body in with_clean_history (or take test_env_lock directly). Audit the whole lib suite for other tests that touch shared chat_history globals (record_turn / clear / recent_turns) or HELIX_CHAT_HISTORY_FILE without the lock — spot-check found production callers in src/io/llm_gemini/mod.rs and src/io/ollama/mod.rs, so check whether any of their tests drive those paths concurrently. Consider making the temp file name unique per test (e.g. include the test name), not just per pid, as defense in depth.\n\nNOTE: full `cargo test` verification is still gated on task 262 (installer include_str! blocks all non-lib test targets). Verify via cargo test --lib until 262 lands.\n\nSURVEYOR 1 VERIFIED 2026-10-16 (plan only, no code touched):\n- clear_empties_history (src/chat_history.rs:265) is the ONLY chat_history test outside with_clean_history (line 185); all 8 others hold test_env_lock (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs:591, process-global Mutex) for the whole test body.\n- Audit: NO other test in the lib suite calls record_turn / clear / load_from_disk / recent_turns, and NO test outside chat_history.rs sets HELIX_CHAT_HISTORY_FILE (grep-verified). llm_gemini test gemini_tool_loop_emits_spawn_subagent_call calls call_gemini_tools, which READS recent_turns (mod.rs:387) but never writes — and it holds test_env_lock, so it is serialized with the chat_history tests. record_turn in llm_gemini lives in handle_gemini_bus_message (mod.rs:68), which no test calls. Ollama tests are pure unit tests + one #[ignore]d live test (test_handle_ollama_live); no default-suite ollama test drives handle_ollama_message / call_ollama_tools (the record_turn / recent_turns sites, mod.rs:332/553). No audit changes needed beyond the 263.2 fix.\n- Second failure direction: clear_empties_history's record_turn(\"x\",\"y\") also APPENDS to whatever HELIX_CHAT_HISTORY_FILE points to at that moment — another test's shared temp file (inflating its count) or, with the var unset, the real logs/chat_history.jsonl (a stray untracked logs/chat_history.jsonl is in the worktree; Ranger to check whether it is test pollution and remove it if so).\n- Unique-per-test temp filenames are OPTIONAL defense-in-depth only: they fix the disk side, NOT the shared in-memory HISTORY — clear() would still wipe global memory without the lock. Do not ship filenames as the fix.\n- Do NOT change production record_turn / clear / load_from_disk / recent_turns — test-only fix. Do NOT re-plan 261/262.",
      "testStrategy": "263.1: repro attempt logged (loop counts + outcome; attempt counts even if the flake doesn't fire). 263.2-263.3: cargo test --lib chat_history green. 263.4: cargo test --lib loop 10x at default parallelism green + cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1 green. Full cargo test re-verification deferred until task 262 lands (262 gates all non-lib test targets).",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "263.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Reproduce the flake (attempt): loop cargo test --lib chat_history (50x) + full cargo test --lib (20x); log attempts; proceed on the verified mechanism if it doesn't fire"
        },
        {
          "id": "263.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Fix clear_empties_history isolation: wrap its body in with_clean_history (src/chat_history.rs:265) so it runs under test_env_lock"
        },
        {
          "id": "263.3",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Audit: confirm no other test touches shared chat_history globals or HELIX_CHAT_HISTORY_FILE without the lock (llm_gemini read-only under lock; ollama live test ignored) + check stray logs/chat_history.jsonl"
        },
        {
          "id": "263.4",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Verify: cargo test --lib loop 10x green at default parallelism + single-threaded run green; leave changes uncommitted for QM/John review"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 264,
      "title": "Fix parse_mail_list dropping numeric UIDs: support watcher never sees mail",
      "description": "The support watcher polls run and mail-mcp returns mail, but parse_mail_list() drops every message: mail-mcp mail_search emits numeric UIDs ({\"uid\": <u32>}) while the parser only accepts STRING id/uid/message_id. The numeric-uid fallback looks for an \"id\" key that mail_search never emits, yields None, and the message is silently discarded. Result: seen_ids stays empty, no drafts, no auto-send, despite mail_configured=true and a healthy mailbox.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "FILED BY COBBLE JR per John, 2026-10-16 evening live drill. FOR RANGER 1.\n\nROOT CAUSE (verified 2026-10-16 ~21:27 EDT):\n- mail-mcp mail_search (~/workspace/mail-mcp/src/mail.rs blocking_search) returns {\"mailbox\",\"criteria\",\"returned\",\"messages\":[{\"uid\": <u32>, \"subject\", \"from\", \"date\"}]}. uid is a JSON NUMBER. Params default sanely: mailbox=INBOX, query=\"\" -> criteria ALL, limit default 10; the watcher calls with {\"limit\": 50}, so the call itself is fine.\n- Helix parse_mail_list (src/support_watch/mod.rs:201) per item: get(\"id\") -> None (mail_search never emits \"id\"); or_else get(\"uid\") -> Some(number); and_then as_str() -> None (number, not string); or_else get(\"id\").as_u64() -> None (no \"id\" key) -> `?` -> None -> item DROPPED. The as_u64 fallback only helps when the key is literally \"id\" AND numeric; it never helps for \"uid\"/\"message_id\".\n- Top-level \"messages\" wrapper IS handled, so the drop is purely per-item id typing.\n\nEVIDENCE CHAIN (all verified live on R630, Helix PID 54523 after debug restart):\n- GET /support/status -> mail_configured: true (resolve_mail_tools() succeeds in-process; watcher HAS check+send tools). No-tools theory DEAD.\n- Config valid: TOML OK, [mcp] enabled=true, [[mcp.servers]] google + mail each with own [mcp.servers.env]. Binary fresh (Oct 16 00:50, has watcher strings). CWD /home/cobble/helix. main.rs resolves config_path_used=\"config.toml\", mcp_config_path same file. Format check: tool_definitions() returns Ollama-style {function:{name}} matching the watcher's expectation.\n- Polls run (state.json last_check advances), seen_ids=[], unhandled=[], draft_attempts={}. Test mail (\"Hi\"/\"Test\", from John's phone) sat unread in support@ INBOX all day through business-hours 5-min polls.\n- Mock E2E (task 260.1) passed because the MOCK returns string ids, masking the real-server shape. The mock must be fixed to emit numeric uids (264.3) or this class of bug recurs.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (264.1): in parse_mail_list, accept numeric id/uid/message_id by stringifying the u64 (e.g. v.as_str().map(str::to_string).or_else(|| v.as_u64().map(|n| n.to_string()))) instead of mapping numeric to \"\" and dropping. Keep string ids working; keep dropping items with no id at all.\n\nDOWNSTREAM COMPATIBILITY (verify in 264.4): IncomingMail.id flows to state seen/unhandled lists and to the drafter -> mail_read / mail_modify paths, which expect a numeric UID. A stringified \"123\" must parse back to u32 there. Confirm mail_read takes the id as uid (check drafter.rs/drafts.rs call sites); if any site assumes the id is already numeric-typed, adapt it to parse. Do NOT change mail-mcp: its numeric uid output is correct IMAP behavior.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE: Helix installs no logger (no env_logger/set_logger/SimpleLogger/tracing_subscriber init anywhere in src/), so all log:: output is discarded. That is a separate observability defect, NOT this task. Do not bundle it here; file separately.\n\nR630 STATE NOTES: debug override staged at /etc/systemd/system/helix.service.d/debug.conf (RUST_LOG=debug) during diagnosis — it never produced watcher logs (no logger installed) and should be removed + service restarted when this fix deploys. Test mail still unread in support@ INBOX for the post-fix live drill. state.json was reset during diagnosis (backup in /tmp/support_watch-state-before-debug.bak on R630).\n\nRESULTS (Ranger 1, 2026-10-16):\n264.1: parse_mail_list id extraction rewritten — one lookup over id/uid/message_id, accept string OR u64 (stringified). Doc comment updated.\n264.2: new test parse_mail_list_accepts_numeric_uids_like_real_mail_search — real mail_search payload shape (messages wrapper, numeric uid 123, from with display name), numeric id + message_id variants, string-id still works, null-id / id-less items still drop.\n264.3: mock E2E stub now emits the real mail_search shape ({\"messages\":[{\"uid\":4242,...}]}) ; id asserts updated \"mock-1\" -> \"4242\".\n264.4: downstream verified by inspection — msg.id flows only as String (in_reply_to, WatchState seen/unhandled sets, mark_handled string ops). No parse::<u32> on the id anywhere in drafter.rs/drafts.rs; no mail_read/mail_modify uid call exists in the watcher flow yet. Stringified numeric uid is fully compatible. The mock E2E with id \"4242\" exercises the full loop as executable proof.\n264.5: cargo test --lib support_watch: 49 passed, 0 failed. Full cargo test --lib: 424 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored (was 423; +1 new regression test). Changes left UNCOMMITTED for review. Live drill on R630 after John deploys (test mail still unread) completes 255.3/260.2/260.3.\nNote: this resolves the reviewer's deferred nit B4 from the ranger-255-260 review (\"numeric message ids still dropped\").\n",
      "testStrategy": "264.1-264.2: new unit test feeds parse_mail_list the REAL mail_search payload shape ({\"messages\":[{\"uid\":123,\"subject\":\"Hi\",\"from\":\"john mcconnell <...>\",\"date\":\"...\"}]}) and asserts the message is returned with id \"123\"; plus numeric \"id\" and \"message_id\" variants and the existing string-id cases. 264.3: mock E2E emits numeric uids; suite still green. 264.4: downstream id->uid parse covered by existing drafter/drafts tests or a new assertion. 264.5: cargo test --lib support_watch green + full lib suite green; leave changes uncommitted for review. Live drill on R630 after John deploys (test mail still unread) completes tasks 255.3/260.2/260.3.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "264.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Fix parse_mail_list (src/support_watch/mod.rs:201) to accept numeric id/uid/message_id by stringifying the u64 instead of dropping"
        },
        {
          "id": "264.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Regression test: parse_mail_list on real mail_search payload (numeric uid, messages wrapper) returns the message with id \"123\"; cover numeric id + message_id variants + string-id cases"
        },
        {
          "id": "264.3",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Fix mock E2E (task 260.1) to emit numeric uids like real mail-mcp so the mock cannot mask this shape mismatch again"
        },
        {
          "id": "264.4",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Verify downstream id flow: stringified uid parses back to u32 in drafter/mail_read/mail_modify/mark_handled paths; adapt any site that assumes numeric-typed id"
        },
        {
          "id": "264.5",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Verify: cargo test --lib support_watch green + full lib suite green; leave changes uncommitted for review; live drill on R630 after John deploys"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 265,
      "title": "Install a logger and audit logging project-wide: log:: output is currently discarded everywhere",
      "description": "Helix installs no logger, so every log::info!/debug!/warn!/error! call in the codebase is a silent no-op and RUST_LOG has no effect. This made the support-watcher outage (task 264) undiagnosable from logs: zero mcp: spawn lines, zero support_watch: lines at any level, even with RUST_LOG=debug in effect. Install a logger honoring RUST_LOG and put logging where it is needed across the whole project, without leaking secrets.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "FILED BY COBBLE JR per John, 2026-10-16 evening drill (follow-up to task 264). FOR RANGER 1.\n\nROOT (verified 2026-10-16): grep for env_logger/set_logger/SimpleLogger/tracing_subscriber init across ~/helix/src/ returns NOTHING. The log facade IS used widely (support_watch mod.rs info!/debug!/warn!, mcp_client try_execute warn!, etc.) but nothing sinks it. Startup println! lines reach the journal; log:: lines do not. A debug restart with RUST_LOG=debug in effect produced zero watcher/MCP lines — the debug override was working (systemctl show Environment confirmed RUST_LOG=debug), the logger simply did not exist.\n\n265.1 INSTALL LOGGER: add env_logger (log-facade-compatible; do NOT migrate the codebase to tracing — bigger change, out of scope) to Cargo.toml; initialize once, early in main() before run_helix (and in any lib/bin entry that needs it). Honor RUST_LOG with a sane default (info). Init must be idempotent-safe (try_init or OnceLock guard) so tests cannot panic on double init. Verify per-module filtering works (e.g. RUST_LOG=helix::support_watch=debug). env_logger writes to stderr, which systemd forwards to the journal — no extra plumbing needed.\n\n265.2 AUDIT + ADD LOGGING PROJECT-WIDE: every silent fallback / swallowed error gets at least a warn!:\n- McpConfig::load_from_toml falling back to the disabled default (log the path + that MCP is disabled — this silent fallback sent the 264 diagnosis down the wrong path for hours).\n- load_config read failures; manager() returning None; MCP spawn/handshake/tools-list failures; tool call errors (try_execute already warn!s — confirm it fires post-logger).\n- Watcher poll outcomes (info!/debug! lines already exist — confirm they appear), cadence/mode transitions, draft attempts/failures.\n- Config path resolution, config save/load failures, web server errors, agent/tool errors, backup/restore outcomes.\nUse appropriate levels: error for failures, warn for fallbacks/degraded operation, info for lifecycle, debug for per-call detail. Keep debug! out of tight loops.\n\n265.3 SECRETS HYGIENE (mandatory review pass): never log secret VALUES — [mcp.servers.env] values (MAIL_PASS, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, tokens), auth tokens, customer mail bodies/subjects, full config dumps. Log keys/paths/counts, never values. Grep log macros near secret-bearing variables and fix any that leak. A debug log that prints a mailbox password is worse than no log.\n\n265.4 PRINTLN POLICY: decide and document (short comment in main.rs or task notes): println! stays for user-facing CLI output (startup banner, \"Using config file\"); diagnostics go through log::. Convert existing diagnostic println!/eprintln! to log:: where they are diagnostics, not user output. Do not churn user-facing output for style.\n\n265.5 VERIFY + DEPLOY NOTE: cargo test --lib green (no test broken by logger init; tests capturing output still pass). R630 manual verification after John deploys: restart with RUST_LOG=debug, journalctl shows support_watch + mcp: lines; restart at info shows info+warn only, debug filtered out. DEPLOY NOTE: a debug override is currently staged on R630 at /etc/systemd/system/helix.service.d/debug.conf (RUST_LOG=debug) from the 264 diagnosis — it does nothing until this task lands, then it will FLOOD the journal. Removing that override + restarting at info is part of this task's deploy.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: rewording log messages everywhere for style; structured/JSON logging (future work if wanted); log rotation (journald handles it); the task 264 parser fix itself.\n\nRESULTS (Ranger 1, 2026-10-16):\n265.1: env_logger was ALREADY a Cargo dependency (0.11.11) but never initialized. Added helix::init_logging() in src/lib.rs (env_logger::Builder::from_env, default filter info, try_init for idempotency) + unit test proving idempotent + logger-live marker. main.rs calls it first thing in main(), before the ACP branch (env_logger writes to stderr, so ACP JSON-RPC on stdout stays clean). installer.rs/test_ollama.rs use no log:: macros, so no init needed there. Verified: RUST_LOG=off suppresses the marker, RUST_LOG=helix::tests=debug shows it; marker format '[ts INFO helix::tests] ...'.\n265.2: config::load_section helper (src/config/mod.rs) — all 8 section loaders (mcp/acp/shell/ssh/okf/reasoning/project_scanner/support) funnel through it: unparseable TOML -> warn + defaults; missing section -> debug + defaults; wrong shape -> warn + defaults. mcp_client load_config_from read failure -> warn; manager() None -> debug (not warn: fires per call, off is the normal state). MCP manager spawn/list/call failures ALREADY warn! (were just invisible). Watcher poll outcomes ALREADY info!/debug!. tools::execute injection guard ALREADY warn!. Web server: warn! on config_save/manifest_save auth rejection, merge-base read failure, REDACTED refusal, TOML rejection, write failures. chat_history compaction write failure -> eprintln once (module's idiom). cpu nightly_report + persist_consolidated_memory write failures -> warn!. Installer backup_existing ALREADY println!/eprintln!s. Deliberately untouched: WS/channel-send `let _ =` (receiver-gone is normal; logging would spam), test cleanup remove_dir_all, cpu fix-loop fire-and-forget shell calls (outcome is logged), bus.publish ignores.\n265.3: secrets audit fixed 15 sites to metadata-only (names/keys/paths/counts/lengths): runtime_loop ToolCall args -> arg keys, FinalAnswer/Planner Error/Replan -> lengths, tool-success value -> length; llm_gemini + ollama tool-error warns -> lengths; unix_socket CLI args -> key count/char count; web_server chat msg -> msg_len (info! + println); mcp_handler bus error data -> length; ACP dispatch -> static warn; instructions/interrupts bus messages -> from/to/data_len (both log:: and log_to_file sinks); bus log_transaction -> metadata-only (was first 300 chars of every payload into TRACKED logs/bus_log.md); drafts.rs send-result 200 chars -> length; cpu commands agent.run result -> length; Instruction Debug dump (carried memory values/bus payloads/skill args/LLM prompts) -> new Instruction::variant_name(); bus NO SUBSCRIBER println data preview (120 chars) deleted (eprintln with metadata already covers it); io.rs + terminal placeholder handlers full message.data -> metadata. Parser/serde errors are NEVER logged with {e}: their Display echoes the offending file line/value (config TOML parse + load_section shape errors log static hints only). io::Error-only warns kept (no values). Deliberately KEPT: email_tools to/subject sent-mail audit trail (recipient+subject prove delivery; not a secret value or body), four error!(\"{}\", error_msg) sites (locally-formatted io/channel errors, no untrusted content).\n265.4: policy documented in main.rs comment (println!/eprintln! = user-facing CLI only; log:: = all server diagnostics; never log content). Converted server diagnostics to log::: web_server chat line -> info!, ollama SUCCESS -> info!, ollama FAILED println duplicate deleted (warn! above covers it), cpu error-log review -> info!. Deliberately LEFT as println!/eprintln! for a follow-up cleanup (no content in any of them): main.rs startup banner + 'Using config file', ACP CLI messages, bus lifecycle lines, io routing lines, cpu routine/heartbeat/memory-consolidation lines, hy_evo chaos/visualization, terminal interface start, unix_cli docs, installer bin output, chat_history eprintln!s (module idiom). Test-only println!s left (ollama live-test response print).\n265.5: cargo check --lib clean (4 remaining warnings all pre-existing: unix_socket unused, ops_restart state = task 254). cargo check --all-targets clean (exit 0; router/mod.rs unused-import warnings pre-existing = task 254). cargo test --lib: 425 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored (was 424 after 264; +1 init_logging test). RUST_LOG filtering verified live (off suppresses, module filter shows). Secrets re-grep clean (one hit = backend name only). Changes left UNCOMMITTED for review. R630 deploy note: REMOVE /etc/systemd/system/helix.service.d/debug.conf + restart at info when this lands, or debug will flood the journal. Side observation: test runs appended new metadata-only lines to the already-dirty tracked logs/bus_log.md (old content-preview lines in the diff are pre-existing, not mine); left untouched rather than restoring and destroying pre-existing local content.\n",
      "testStrategy": "265.1-265.2: cargo test --lib green; new test asserting logger init is safe to call (try_init / once semantics) if feasible without global-state flakiness; existing watcher/MCP tests still pass with a logger installed. 265.3: secrets grep pass clean (no log macro adjacent to secret values). 265.5: R630 manual — RUST_LOG=debug shows support_watch + mcp: lines in journalctl; RUST_LOG=info filters debug out; debug override removed, service restarted at info.",
      "subtasks": [
