      "id": 276,
      "title": "Nightly error-log review counts all CPU chatter as errors; count real/recent errors and rotate the log",
      "description": "routine_error_log_review (src/cpu/mod.rs) counts every non-empty line of error_log.md as an 'error line' with no date filter and no ERROR-pattern match, and nothing rotates the file. log_to_file (src/utils.rs) appends all CPU chatter (TRACE, routine_run ticks, polls, scheduler, executor starts) to ~/.helix/logs/error_log.md, which grew ~54k lines/day (~37/min) after the 2026-10-20 reinstall: 322,685 lines by 2026-10-26, vs the 265,352 the alert reported the night before. Any total > 0 fires the same bus error alert, so it now fires every night and grows forever; and maybe_nightly_fix (1-7am window + [shell] enabled on the R630) arms on these chatter lines and attempts fixes on junk. The web UI /logs/error/clear endpoint clears only state.logging.error_log (the 1-line runtime file), NOT the ~/.helix file the review actually counts, and writes back an INIT line that itself counts as an 'error line'.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "DIAGNOSED 2026-10-26 from John's R630 output: wc -l ~/helix/logs/error_log.md (1 line) vs ~/.helix/logs/error_log.md (322,685 lines); tail = per-minute support-mail-watch routine_run lines; file created by installer 2026-10-20 20:36 EDT. R630 Helix log timestamps are UTC (4h ahead of EDT).\n\nCHANGES:\n1. check_error_logs: count only genuine errors - either lines carrying an error marker, or lines from the last 24h (log lines carry '[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS AM/PM]' timestamps; parse and filter). Prefer last-24h + error-marker filtering; implementer's call on the exact predicate, but chatter-only fixtures must count 0.\n2. Cap/rotate ~/.helix/logs/error_log.md (e.g. keep last N lines or daily rotation with archive) so the file cannot grow unboundedly; keep an INIT-style marker that the review skips.\n3. Alert gating falls out of (1): bus error fires only when the FILTERED count > 0. State it explicitly in the report body (filtered count + file sizes).\n4. Fix /logs/error/clear to clear the file log_to_file actually writes (and both review candidates), and do not write back an INIT line the review counts - or make the review skip INIT lines.\n5. Consequence: maybe_nightly_fix then arms only on real errors.\n\nCLEARING (done 2026-10-26 night by John on the R630: backup + truncate both files) resets the baseline but does NOT silence the alert - the file regrows ~54k/day and any total > 0 alerts. This task is the actual fix.\n\nDo NOT delete the log without backup; do NOT change the support-watch cadence (the ticks are legitimate routine chatter, not the bug).",
      "testStrategy": "Fixture error_log.md files mixing chatter (routine_run, TRACE, poll, scheduler, executor starts) + genuine error lines + lines older than 24h: assert filtered count equals genuine recent errors only; chatter-only fixture counts 0 and fires no bus alert; rotation caps the file at the configured bound; existing tests error_log_check_reports_findings_on_fixture, error_log_check_handles_missing_log, error_review_reports_and_stays_propose_only_off_hours stay green; cargo test --lib exit 0.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "276.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "check_error_logs: filter to genuine recent errors (error marker and/or last-24h timestamp parse); report filtered count + file sizes"
        },
        {
          "id": "276.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Cap/rotate ~/.helix/logs/error_log.md; review skips INIT lines"
        },
        {
          "id": "276.3",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Fix /logs/error/clear to clear the file log_to_file writes (both review candidates), no counted INIT line written back"
        },
        {
          "id": "276.4",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Fixture tests (chatter-only = 0, no alert; mixed + old lines filtered; rotation bound) + CHANGELOG entry"
        }
      ]
    },
