      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nLog line per collection cycle: `self_improve: metrics ...` (counts only, metadata-only — same rule as task 278). New route GET /self_improve/status in src/io/web_server/mod.rs beside /support/status (route at :459, handler support_status ~:1973 at c7ecc41 is the pattern to copy), returning the latest ledger entry + current phase + kill-switch states + budget counters. DELIBERATE HARDENING vs /support/status: the new endpoint sits BEHIND require_web_token (src/io/web_server/mod.rs:521) — loop internals are not public. No mutating endpoints in this phase. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: status_snapshot() in mod.rs (phase, enabled, kill_switches{config_enabled,stop_file_present,routine_enabled}, budgets{4 limits + proposals_open}, latest_ledger), GET /self_improve/status on the PROTECTED router (require_web_token middleware — deliberately hardened vs public /support/status), handler beside support_status. 1 new route test green (401 no token, 401 wrong token, 200 + full shape with a staged ledger cycle). SIDE EFFECT: the 2 dead-code warnings from 277 (runtime_dir/live_config) are now RESOLVED — status_snapshot consumes both — so cargo check --lib is back to zero warnings a task early (before 281). No mutating endpoints added.",
