      "description": "Produce the one-week ledger export + gap detector; John reads it and agrees or corrects what 'normal' looks like. Phase 1 does not start until this passes.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nRanger 1: (1) run collection for 7 consecutive days with the routine enabled by John in collect mode (phase=0 — see task 281's seeding; the routine ships disabled, John enables it); (2) gap-detector check: one ledger entry per scheduled cycle, zero qm_missing gaps (or gaps explicitly explained); (3) export the week as a readable summary for John (per-metric normals: routine failure rate, watcher stats, filtered error counts, restarts). JOHN'S EYEBALL REQUIRED: John reads the export and confirms or corrects 'normal'; record his sign-off (date + note) in the task results. If the ledger has gaps, Phase 1 does not start — fix the collector and re-run the week. Update CHANGELOG.md.",
