    {
      "dependencies": [
        277,
        278
      ],
      "description": "Seed the nightly self-improve routine (disabled by default) and its CPU handler: kill-switch checks first, phase gate, ledger read, worst-signature pick, one worker dispatch.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nSeed in default_routines() (src/cron/registry.rs:195+): id \"self-improve\", name \"Self-improvement loop\", schedule \"daily 03:30\" (off-hours; avoids 02:00 memory consolidation and 06:30 error_log_review), enabled=false (fail-closed — John enables via the existing routine toggle, cf. the mail_check precedent at registry.rs:225; the loop must never re-enable itself). The existing seed-merge path (load_or_seed, registry.rs:276-290: missing defaults are appended to existing routines.json files without touching John's choices) carries the routine to the R630's existing file — verify that pickup in a test with a pre-existing routines.json.\n\nHandler arm in handle_routine_run (src/cpu/mod.rs:436, beside the :445 support-mail-watch arm): (1) kill-switch checks FIRST (task 284's checks — the handler calls them; if tripped, log which condition and abort); (2) phase gate: phase 0 → collect-only (call collect_cycle, return, propose nothing); phase >= 1 → proceed; (3) read the ledger, pick the single worst failing signature under budgets (task 283's pre-check); (4) dispatch ONE worker sub-agent via dispatch_spawn (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs:362) with SpawnSpec{backend: draft backend per D3, role_hint: loop-worker, timeout_secs <= max_cycle_minutes*60}; (5) record the outcome.\n\nNON-GOAL GUARDRAIL (do not blur): the loop never invokes maybe_nightly_fix (src/cpu/mod.rs:745) or its paths. That separate John-granted nighttime autonomy is untouched by this build; the loop proposes only. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: routine seed (self-improve, daily 03:30, enabled=false) in default_routines — existing load_or_seed merge carries it to older deployments untouched; CPU arm in handle_routine_run + routine_self_improve: kill switches FIRST, collect from live sources (counts only, never ErrorFindings.recent), ledger append + counts-only log line, phase-0 collect-only return, phase>=1 + failing signal dispatches EXACTLY ONE worker (SpawnSpec backend=draft_backend, role_hint=loop-worker, timeout=max_cycle_minutes*60). Never touches maybe_nightly_fix. 5 new tests green (2 registry: seeded-disabled + merge-pickup preserving John's choices; 3 CPU: phase-0 collects/proposes nothing, kill-tripped aborts before dispatch with empty registry, phase-1 on restart signal dispatches exactly one loop-worker). cargo check --lib zero warnings. SEQUENCING NOTE: the worker's tight allowlist + proposal record arrive in 282 and budget gating in 283; the 281 dispatch is real but unconstrained until 282 lands — safe because the routine ships disabled.",
      "id": 281,
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "done",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "dependencies": [],
          "id": "281.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Routine seed (disabled) + merge-pickup test"
