      "testStrategy": "Tests: handler with phase=0 collects and proposes nothing; kill-switch tripped aborts before dispatch (assert dispatch_spawn not called); seeded default routine is present with enabled=false; a pre-existing routines.json gains the routine via the merge path without touching existing choices; dispatch arm routes \"self-improve\" correctly. cargo check --lib zero new warnings; lib suite green.",
      "title": "Loop Phase 1: self-improve routine + cycle handler (phase-gated)"
    },
    {
      "dependencies": [
        281
      ],
      "description": "The worker sub-agent's brief and tool allowlist, and the task-list-shaped proposal record with the mandatory trace field that enforces the spec's R3 rule.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nWorker brief (system-prompt text stored in code, versioned): role = propose-only loop worker. Allowed tools = read tools + worktree write tools + git-wrapper tools (Phase 2) + proposal-file write. FORBIDDEN: shell outside the worktree, send tools, live-tree tools, spawn_subagent (already absolute-excluded at src/persona.rs:246 — an allowlist can never re-add it). Enforce via the existing persona allowlist mechanism (src/persona.rs:243-292: frontmatter allowlist filtering at dispatch; unknown tools ignored with a warning; a zero-match allowlist is rejected).\n\nProposal record in the RUNTIME dir at rt_dir/self_improve/proposals.json — NOT the repo .zed/task_list.json (writing the repo's task list would be a live-tree write; the spec's 'task-list-shaped entries' means the shape, not the file). Fields: problem_statement, trace (failing test name OR metric key — REQUIRED), diff_description (Phase 1: description only, no branch yet), proving_test, signature, status (proposed), created_at, budget-check refs.\n\nR3 RULE (spec risk R3 — logs/messages/chat can carry planted instructions): a proposal whose rationale traces to message/log/chat content rather than a failing test or a metric is auto-rejected at intake. Implement trace validation: the trace must match a known failing test name (from ledger/QM data) or a known metric key; free-text 'someone said' traces are rejected. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: worker.rs — LOOP_WORKER_TOOLS (8 read-only tools), filter_loop_worker_tools (intersect + fail-closed Err on zero match, spawn_subagent never re-addable), interposed in run_subagent for role loop-worker only; agents/loop-worker.md shipped in repo + ensure_loop_worker_persona seeds it into rt/agents/ (never overwrites John's edits); build_loop_brief moved from CPU handler into worker.rs. ProposalRecord + intake_proposal in rt/self_improve/proposals.json (NOT repo task list — live-tree write avoided) with R3 trace validation (exact metric key from latest ledger, exact known test name from prior proposals, or test-shaped name; free-text/missing/empty auto-rejected) and budget refs at intake. 7/7 worker tests + 3 CPU handler tests green, zero warnings. CLARIFICATIONS: (1) R3 'known test name' at intake is shape + prior-proposal membership — existence is verified by the Phase 2 evaluator running the test (intake cannot verify without running cargo); (2) Gemini draft path takes no tool definitions today, so on Gemini the binding constraint is brief+persona text while the filter still refuses zero-match spawns on any backend and fully binds the Ollama tool path; (3) budget refs count PRIOR proposals at intake (283's gate counts prior+1).",
      "id": 282,
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "done",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "dependencies": [],
          "id": "282.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Worker brief + allowlist enforcement"
        },
        {
          "dependencies": [
            "282.1"
          ],
          "id": "282.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Proposal record + R3 trace validation at intake"
        }
      ],
      "testStrategy": "Tests: allowlist filters to exactly the permitted set; spawn_subagent cannot be re-added via allowlist; proposal intake accepts a test-traced proposal and rejects a message-content-traced one; missing/empty trace rejected; proposals.json round-trip. cargo check --lib zero new warnings; lib suite green.",
      "title": "Loop Phase 1: worker brief, tight allowlist, proposal record (R3 trace rule)"
    },
    {
      "dependencies": [
        281,
        282
      ],
      "description": "Enforce the spec's budgets as code: 3 proposals/week, 1 open/signature, 60-min cycle, 500-line diff cap, 30-day declined / 7-day failed-eval cooldowns, dedupe by signature.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nNew file src/self_improve/budgets.rs: rolling 3-proposals/week counter (from proposals.json); 1-open-proposal-per-signature check (dedupe by failing test name / metric key); cycle wall-clock cap 60 min enforced via timeout around the worker dispatch (timeout → abandon worktree, record cycle_timeout, no partial proposal); 500-line diff cap — SPLIT ENFORCEMENT, stated explicitly so Ranger 1 does not invent a Phase 1 diff measurer: Phase 1 records a diff-size estimate field at intake, but the cap is enforced HARD in Phase 2's evaluator (task 287) where a real diff exists; cooldowns: declined → 30 days, failed-eval → 7 days without a changed failing signature (checked against proposals.json outcomes + timestamps); lesson recording via memory_continuity record_lesson / record_important_outcome (src/agents/memory_continuity.rs:88/105) for accepted/rejected shapes so repeat shapes stop. Any budget violation aborts the cycle with a logged reason — per spec, a cycle that violates a budget fails the PHASE, not just the cycle, so log it as phase_failure, never a quiet skip. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: budgets.rs — check_proposal_allowed (weekly cap prior+1>=max, 1-open-per-signature dedupe, declined 30d cooldown, failed-eval 7d cooldown per-signature with changed-signature bypass), CycleDeadline (max_cycle_minutes), lesson/outcome recording via memory_continuity. Handler restructured (281-order refinement): ledger entry now written AFTER the worker completes so the cycle outcome (proposal:<sig> / phase_failure:<reason> / cycle_timeout / parse_failed) is recorded IN the entry; violations logged as phase_failure, never quiet skips; timeout abandons with no partial proposal. 5/5 budget unit tests green (4th-week blocked, 2nd-open blocked, declined 29d blocked/31d allowed, failed-eval 6d blocked/8d allowed + changed-sig bypass, deadline expiry) + 36 self-improve + 3 CPU handler tests green, zero warnings. DEVIATIONS: (1) cooldowns run from ProposalRecord.updated_at (status-change time, new field) not intake time — required for correct semantics; (2) lesson recording does NOT use Cpu.state — there are two AgentState types and Cpu.state is runtime counters, not the continuity type — so lessons go through a fresh unified AgentState + persist_memory_deltas into self.memory (task-206 pattern); (3) parse_worker_report added to worker.rs (Phase 1 path completion — without it the handler could never intake worker output); (4) 500-line cap NOT enforced here — recorded as estimate at intake, enforced hard in 287 per task details.",
      "id": 283,
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "done",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "dependencies": [],
          "id": "283.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Counters + dedupe + cooldowns"
