      "testStrategy": "Tests: 4th proposal in a week blocked; second open proposal for the same signature blocked; declined signature re-proposed at 29 days blocked, at 31 days allowed; failed-eval at 6 days blocked, at 8 days allowed (unchanged signature); changed signature bypasses the failed-eval cooldown; cycle timeout abandons cleanly with no partial proposal. cargo check --lib zero new warnings; lib suite green.",
      "title": "Loop Phase 1: budget, cooldown, and lesson engine (hard caps)"
    },
    {
      "dependencies": [
        277,
        281
      ],
      "description": "Implement the spec's three independent kill mechanisms (D6, all confirmed) with logging of which condition stopped the cycle.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nChecks run at the TOP of every cycle handler invocation, before any work, and the handler calls them before the phase gate: (1) config [self_improve] enabled=false → abort; (2) SELF_IMPROVE_OFF stop file present in the runtime dir → abort before any work, with NO 'finish the current cycle' exception for cycles that would write outside the worktree (worktree writes in flight are abandoned with the worktree — implement the abort path to drop the worktree handle and run cleanup); (3) routine disabled via registry set_enabled (src/cron/registry.rs:322) → scheduler stops firing, and the handler re-checks enabled as belt-and-braces. Any ONE of the three suffices. Every abort logs WHICH condition stopped it (config / stop-file / routine-disabled) so John can tell a kill from a crash. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: kill switch complete — check_kill_switches (config/stop-file/routine, in that order) + kill_abort_message (line always names the condition) in mod.rs, handler aborts before any work, main.rs sets self_improve runtime dir (completing 279's production wiring). 6 CPU handler tests (config-disabled, routine-disabled, stop-file aborts; mid-cycle stop aborts NEXT cycle with no proposal orphan; re-enable resumes) + 6 mod tests (3 mechanisms + all-clear + abort-message naming + read-only routines flag) green, zero warnings. SPEC READING: a stop file appearing DURING a cycle aborts the NEXT cycle — the in-flight cycle's handler-side intake stands (its worktree-write abandonment is 287's cleanup, since Phase 1 has no worktrees). Phase 0+1 committed in branch ranger-loop-277-291.",
