      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nRanger 1: run the loop nightly for 2 consecutive weeks (phase=1, routine enabled by John). Collect evidence: cycle logs (kill-switch states, budget counters), proposals.json (≤3/week), live-tree cleanliness proof (live checkout git status clean of loop files — the loop writes only the runtime dir + worktrees), send audit (bus-log grep for loop-origin sends = 0). JOHN'S EYEBALL REQUIRED: John reads the proposals and rates at least one 'actually correct' (quality bar, not volume); record his rating in the task results. A cycle that violates a budget fails the PHASE, not just the cycle — if that happens, fix and restart the 2-week clock. Update CHANGELOG.md.",
