      "description": "The only git capability the loop may use: worktree add, branch, commit-in-worktree, branch -D. Everything else is rejected by construction (spec unknown U3, closed here).",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nNew file src/self_improve/git.rs: run git via std::process::Command (NO new git2 dependency — the allowlist stays auditable in one place) with an argv allowlist: `worktree add`, `branch`, `commit` (cwd forced to the worktree path, never the live checkout), `branch -D` (cleanup). Reject by construction BEFORE spawning: push, merge, checkout, reset --hard, fetch, pull, and any other subcommand; reject escape flags (--git-dir, --work-tree, -C pointing outside the worktree root, --upload-pack, etc.); sanitize env (unset GIT_ASKPASS, force -c credential.helper= so no credential helper can run). Worktree root: rt_dir/self_improve/worktrees/ (from task 277 config). This wrapper is itself security-sensitive: keep it small, fully tested, and reviewed as such. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: git.rs — Command-based wrapper, no git2. validate_argv runs before EVERY spawn: escape flags rejected anywhere (-C, --git-dir, --work-tree, --upload-pack), subcommand allowlist, branch-name safety, '..' rejection. Env sanitized per spawn (GIT_ASKPASS/GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY/GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES removed, credential.helper= forced, local-only commit identity). Typed methods: add_worktree, remove_worktree, create/delete_branch, add_files, commit. 4/4 fixture-repo tests green (end-to-end add->commit->delete with live branch untouched; 20-case rejection table with no side effects; path/cwd escapes; env sanitization), zero warnings. DEVIATIONS (all minimal, documented in code): (1) 'add' allowed with strict in-worktree path validation — without it new-file diffs could never be committed (commit -a covers tracked modifications only); (2) 'worktree remove --force' allowed — cleanup requires remove-then-delete ordering (git refuses branch -D while a worktree holds the branch); (3) branch ops run with cwd=repo (ref-only, never working-tree files) because after worktree removal no worktree cwd exists — commit/add stay pinned to the worktree, never the live checkout. Test fix: raw test git helper strips hostile env vars so the parallel env test cannot pollute fixtures.",
