      "description": "One proposal at a time: disposable worktree at PreRelese tip, apply the diff, run the bounded subset + approved eval set, write the eval report, clean up. Promotion is gated on John's approved eval set (D5).",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nNew file src/self_improve/evaluator.rs: for ONE proposal at a time (max 1 worktree alive — enforced with a lock file + sweep): create a worktree at origin/PreRelese tip via the task-286 wrapper; apply the worker's diff (the worker now writes a real diff, still only inside the worktree); run the bounded subset — `cargo test --lib` for the modules touched by the diff (module list derived from diff paths) PLUS the approved eval set via the task-242 harness (tests/evals.rs, evals/eval-set.md); write the eval report (pass/fail per test, diff stat, runtime) into the proposal record; delete the worktree after evaluation plus a 24h orphan sweep (stale worktree dirs removed, logged).\n\nD5 GATE (explicit, do not soften): the evaluator reads [self_improve] eval_set_approved (default false — task 242's set is DRAFT, John's approval pending). If false, it still runs the subset but marks the proposal promoted=false with reason \"eval-set-not-approved\" and NEVER promotes. If true, promotion requires the full eval set green. The 500-line diff cap (task 283) is enforced HARD here: diff > 500 lines → rejected with reason, no eval run. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: evaluator.rs — evaluate_proposal(repo, rt_dir, cfg, proposal, diff_files, runner, now): pre-eval rejections (empty diff, >500 new-content lines, no worktree/test run), max-1 lock (.eval.lock, 24h-stale replacement), worktree add -> whole-file diff apply (path escapes rejected) -> add+commit via 286 wrapper -> bounded subset per touched module (filter derivation src/x.rs->x::y, mod.rs->parent, non-lib->full suite fallback) -> D5 gate (closed: skip eval set, promoted=false eval-set-not-approved even on green; open: subset+eval green promotes) -> record update (status evaluated/eval-failed, promoted, reason, full report JSON) + upsert + remove-then-delete cleanup + lock drop. TestRunner trait, RealRunner (cargo in worktree, parses test ok/FAILED lines), FakeRunner for tests. 9/9 tests green (green end-to-end with diff stat + cleanup + branch deletion, failing subset, gate-closed never promotes, gate-open promotes, over-cap pre-eval, max-1 refusal, orphan sweep, path escape), zero warnings. NOTES: (1) ProposalRecord gained eval fields (serde defaults, Phase 1 records still parse) + upsert_proposal; open statuses extended with evaluated + needs-human-review; (2) diff format is whole-file writes (git apply excluded from 286 allowlist — adding it would violate 286); (3) RealRunner builds from scratch in fresh worktrees (minutes) — correct but heavy, bounded handler-side by cycle budget; (4) GAP: no task in 277-291 wires a Phase 2 per-cycle handler arm that calls evaluate_proposal — the component is complete and tested, the cycle wiring is flagged as follow-up.",
