      "description": "Build the PR-opening path (branch → PreRelese, eval report in body, self-improve label, QM-regression withdrawal) with runtime PR-opening default OFF per the D1 decision.",
      "details": "HARD RULES (loop spec, non-negotiable — violation fails the task): the loop never merges, never pushes to master, never restarts the service, never writes the live tree or live config, never sends outbound mail/chat.\n\nNew file src/self_improve/pr.rs: open a PR to PreRelese ONLY (target-branch allowlist = [\"PreRelese\"] — master rejected by construction, as is any other target). PR body = full eval report + diff stat + budget/cooldown refs; label `self-improve`. Preconditions checked in code before any open: Phase 2 eval gate passed in full (bounded subset + approved eval set + secrets audit clean — task 288's audit must be clean, not merely absent), AND [self_improve] pr_opening=true (D1 RUNTIME — default false: when false, the path is a queue-only no-op that logs \"pr-opening-disabled\" and leaves the proposal queued; opening requires John's explicit decision to flip the flag, recorded separately). Sensitive-path proposals are NEVER opened by the loop (needs-human-review → queue-only forever; John opens manually).\n\nQM-regression withdrawal: a loop PR flagged as a regression by the external Quartermaster is commented + closed by the loop itself (closing its own PR is allowed; merging is not). Implement close via the GitHub connector path the nightly diagram updater already uses for PR creation — Ranger 1 MUST verify the connector's close capability during build and record the outcome; if close-via-API is unavailable, withdrawal = mark the proposal withdrawn + post the regression note via the available path, and John closes. Update CHANGELOG.md.\n\nRANGER 1 RESULT: RANGER 1: pr.rs — PrPayload (title/body/head/target/labels/signature; body carries eval report per-test results + diff stat + runtime + intake budget refs), target allowlist [PreRelese] only (master rejected by construction), phase3_gate in order (D1 flag -> audit -> eval gate -> D5 currently-open), QueueBackend (pr_queue.jsonl append, no GitHub call in-crate), request_pr_open (disabled logs pr-opening-disabled, zero backend calls, proposal stays evaluated; green opens once + status queued), withdraw_proposal (backend close + withdrawn + regression note; QueueBackend queues a close action for the consumer). CONNECTOR CHECK (live list-tools 2026-10-28, 46 tools): create_pull_request EXISTS, update_pull_request with state open/closed EXISTS (the close path), merge_pull_request exists and is NEVER called by the loop. 7/7 tests green (disabled zero-call, green payload shape, master rejected, needs-human-review never opened — the 288 stub test's gate-level replacement, re-run green — 4 incomplete-gate shapes blocked, withdrawal close+note+persist, queue open+close entries), zero warnings. DEVIATION from 289 dependency: built per parent's explicit order while gate 289 stays pending (recorded, not passed). Also fixed evaluator eval_passed (was left false) + ProposalRecord.notes field for withdrawal notes.",
