    {
      "dependencies": [],
      "description": "Nightly error-log review alerts (5366, then 7021 error lines) are dominated by false positives, and the nightly fixer amplifies them. Oct 30 breakdown on the R630 (the .helix/logs/error_log.md file, 9749 marker-matching lines): 5650 [AgentState] HALTED lines (agent-run termination, not failure), 2979 self_improve metrics lines (match via the routine_failed substring even at routine_failed=0), 1119 nightly fix attempt report lines (quote old ERROR/HALTED lines, re-counted nightly), 1 CPU line. Causal chain Oct 30 (UTC log time): 06:30 review reports 7021, fixer activity 06:35-06:56 logs 6099 HALTED lines in hour 06, next review counts those too, so alerts grow night over night. Open sub-question: why about 6099 agent terminations in one hour when the fixer is bounded to 2 errors times 8 steps.",
      "details": "293.1 Reproduce with fixtures: sample log containing a bare [AgentState] HALTED: Terminal step reached line, a self_improve metrics line with routine_failed=0, a nightly fix attempt line quoting an old ERROR, a genuine ERROR: failure line, and a genuine Failed line. Assert only the genuine lines count. 293.2 Counting exclusions in check_error_logs: skip bare HALTED termination lines (a run ending is not a failure; keep HALTED lines that carry a failure context if any exist), skip self_improve metrics lines, and skip nightly-fix-attempt report lines. Prefer explicit prefix exclusions over changing the marker list, so genuine ERROR:/Failed lines still count. 293.3 Fixer input and volume: maybe_nightly_fix must receive only actionable findings (exclude the three categories above) so it stops chasing terminations and telemetry. Investigate why hour 06 on Oct 30 produced about 6099 HALTED lines against the 2-error by 8-step bound (agent per step, sub-agents, unbounded loop?) and bound it if it is a runaway. 293.4 Rotation check: the log sat at 101,005 lines on Oct 31, over the 100,000-line rotation cap. Verify rotation fires during the nightly review; fix or report if it does not. 293.5 CHANGELOG plus live proof: after deploy to the R630, run the clear endpoint as the live drill still open from task 276, then confirm the next nightly review is quiet or shows only genuine errors. Results (2026-10-31, Ranger 1, branch ranger-293-error-log): prefix exclusions in is_counted_error_line (metrics lines, fix-attempt quotes, benign HALTED reasons Terminal step reached / test termination); other HALTED reasons still count. Fixer input filtering achieved via counting (recent is built from counted lines only) with no separate fixer change. Volume: no runaway proven (all RuntimeLoop drivers single-run-per-call, loop bounded, burst time-boxed to one hour) so no new bound added. Rotation: no code change, 101,005 reading is cap-plus-regrowth per the function's documented worst case. Verified: error-log tests 8/8, full lib 514/0/4 (baseline 513/0/4 + 1), check --lib zero warnings, check --bin helix clean. No merge, no deploy. Remaining for John after deploy: clear-endpoint live drill (open from 276) plus next-nightly-review check; rotation live check is .prev existence / (rotated ...) report line.",
      "id": 293,
      "priority": "medium",
      "status": "done",
