        }
      ],
      "testStrategy": "New fixture tests green (only genuine lines count). Full lib suite at baseline (513 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored) or better. cargo check --lib zero warnings and cargo check --bin helix clean (bin-target bar from Oct 28). Live drill: post-deploy nightly review count drops to genuine errors only.",
      "title": "Error-log review counts agent terminations, metrics lines, and fixer reports as errors"
    },
    {
      "id": 294,
      "title": "Fix parallel-run race in tool_definitions cache-count tests (BUILD_COUNT)",
      "description": "Nightly Quartermaster 2026-11-01: `cargo test --lib` on PreRelese 98dd072 fails under default parallel execution, a different cache-count test each run, while the single-threaded suite is fully green (514 passed / 0 failed / 4 ignored). Root cause is a real double-build race in tool_definitions() plus unlocked test callers (see details). Fix the production single-flight bug and the test isolation so the default parallel run is green. Start from a fresh PreRelese pull on a new branch (NOT the local ranger-275-voice-tuning checkout); PR against PreRelese, never master, no force-push, push only on John's approval.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "FAILURE EVIDENCE. Run 2 (clean full parallel run, exit 101): 'test result: FAILED. 513 passed; 1 failed; 4 ignored' with tools::tests::invalidation_triggers_rebuild panicking at src/tools/mod.rs:678: 'assertion left == right failed: invalidation must trigger exactly one rebuild, left: 2, right: 1'. Run 1 (truncated by a VM reboot mid-suite, but the failure line predates the reboot) failed the sibling test tools::tests::tool_definitions_excluding_uses_cache instead; that test passes in isolation (1/1 ok). Single-threaded full suite: 514 passed / 0 failed / 4 ignored (suite total 518 = prior baseline 517 + 1 new test from PR #35). RULED OUT: (1) NOT a PR #35 regression (it touches error-log review, not the tools cache). (2) NOT a product-code regression in tool_definitions content (single-threaded green, failing test green alone). (3) NOT the reboot (run 2 reproduced cleanly after it).\n\nREFINED MECHANISM (Surveyor 1, 2026-11-01, from reading the code — not a guess). TWO windows, either suffices for count==2, which is why a different count test fails each run:\n(a) DOUBLE-BUILD ON A SHARED CACHE MISS — a genuine production bug, not just a test artifact. src/tools/mod.rs:544-562 tool_definitions(): fast path takes definitions_cache().read(), drops it, builds, then takes .write() to store. Two threads that both miss the cache build concurrently, and BOTH execute the #[cfg(test)] BUILD_COUNT.fetch_add (mod.rs:558). So any locked count test that invalidates and rebuilds while an unlocked test hits the same empty cache can observe 2. Production impact today is wasted work (and a double MCP bridge fetch when MCP is enabled); content stays correct because last-writer-wins with identical input.\n(b) UNLOCKED CALLERS RACING THE LOCKED COUNT TESTS. The three BUILD_COUNT tests (mod.rs:649 cached_definitions_build_once_across_calls, :672 invalidation_triggers_rebuild, :688 tool_definitions_excluding_uses_cache) all hold test_env_lock (src/tools/subagent_tool.rs:591), so they serialize against EACH OTHER — but the lock only helps holders. Tests that call tool_definitions()/tool_definitions_excluding() WITHOUT the lock: src/tools/mod.rs test_tool_definitions_stable_across_calls (:742), test_tool_definitions_is_array (:753), test_scan_projects_tool_is_registered_in_definitions (:808), test_tool_definitions_includes_project_scanner_tools; src/tools/subagent_tool.rs schema_registered_and_execute_dispatched (:656, calls both tool_definitions() and tool_definitions_excluding()). Any of these landing in a count test's invalidate->reset->build->load window inflates the count. Locked invalidators are NOT the culprits on their own: src/mcp_client/mod.rs:308-311, src/acp/agent.rs:280, src/a2a/a2a_handler.rs:402 all run under test_env_lock (via disabled_test_config / hermetic_mcp_disabled); production invalidate sites src/okf/mod.rs:63,302 are not exercised by unlocked tests (only web-server startup calls set_global_librarian). Ranger must still re-audit: grep all test modules for tool_definitions / tool_definitions_excluding / execute / spawn_subagent callers (also check src/persona.rs, src/io/llm_gemini/mod.rs, src/io/ollama/mod.rs, src/acp/tools.rs, src/support_watch) and lock any found unlocked.\n\nSCOPE GUARD: cache-test race ONLY. Do NOT touch task 262 (installer include_str) or task 273 (unused imports) scope. Baseline to preserve: cargo check --lib zero warnings; cargo check --tests exit 101 baseline-identical (only the known 262 errors + 2x 273 warnings); JS voice-tuning test 9/9.\n\nRANGER AUDIT 2026-11-03 (294.1, code inspection + grep; repro loop running separately).\nUNLOCKED test callers of tool_definitions()/excluding() (window b) — to be locked in 294.3:\n1) src/tools/mod.rs tests: test_tool_definitions_stable_across_calls, test_tool_definitions_is_array, test_scan_projects_tool_is_registered_in_definitions, test_tool_definitions_includes_project_scanner_tools.\n2) src/tools/subagent_tool.rs test: schema_registered_and_execute_dispatched (calls both tool_definitions() and tool_definitions_excluding()).\n3) src/persona.rs tests (via subagent_tool_definitions() / tool_definitions_excluding()): unknown_tool_names_warned_and_ignored, empty_after_filter_falls_back_to_full_set, spawn_subagent_never_allowlisted.\nVERIFIED LOCKED: mcp_client disabled_test_config() acquires test_env_lock; acp/agent.rs + a2a/a2a_handler.rs hermetic_mcp_disabled() acquire test_env_lock (and invalidate under it); all other subagent_tool.rs tests hold _tl.\nRULED OUT as racing partners: execute(\"list_tools\") returns a static string (no tool_definitions call), so the execute() tests in mod.rs are not partners; llm_gemini gemini_function_declarations, ollama default_tools, acp/tools catalog fn are production-only with zero test callers; web_server tests use the MCP override, not the tools cache; support_watch has no hits; okf invalidate sites are production-only; no test calls execute(\"spawn_subagent\") directly.\nPRODUCTION FIX AUDIT (294.2): mcp_client::tool_definitions() never calls back into tools::tool_definitions and never takes the definitions_cache lock (test override mutex / TokioMutex manager lock only; disabled in test env so no bridge runs); build_tool_definitions() uses okf try_lock (non-blocking); invalidate is never called from build — holding the definitions_cache write lock across check->build->store introduces no deadlock cycle.",
      "testStrategy": "1) Re-baseline on the fresh PreRelese tip (suite total may have moved past 518 since 98dd072). 2) `cargo test --lib` (default parallel) 3 times consecutively: all green with 0 failed and the re-baselined pass count each time. 3) Single-threaded `cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1` green. 4) New/kept concurrent cache-miss regression test (subtask 294.2) green under parallel runs. 5) `cargo check --lib` zero warnings and `cargo check --tests` still baseline-identical (only known 262/273 issues, no new errors).",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "294.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Reproduce + audit: loop parallel runs; enumerate every unlocked tool_definitions() caller",
          "details": "On a fresh PreRelese pull + new branch (e.g. ranger-294-cache-race): run `cargo test --lib` in a loop (up to 5x), recording which count test fails each time (flaky — non-reproduction in 5 runs does NOT clear the race; the code inspection in task details already proves the double-build window). Also run `cargo test --lib tools::` in a loop. Audit: grep test modules for tool_definitions/tool_definitions_excluding/execute/spawn_subagent callers and record which lack test_env_lock (starting list in task details; check persona, llm_gemini, ollama, acp/tools, support_watch too). Acceptance: a written list of racing partners + either a reproduced failure or a note that reproduction was skipped after N loop runs with the mechanism still standing on code inspection."
        },
        {
          "id": "294.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Deterministic repro + production single-flight fix in tool_definitions()",
          "details": "First write a deterministic repro (keep it as the regression test if stable): a test that, under test_env_lock, invalidates, resets BUILD_COUNT, spawns N threads calling tool_definitions() concurrently, joins them, and asserts BUILD_COUNT == 1 — this must FAIL before the fix and PASS after. Then fix src/tools/mod.rs tool_definitions() (:544-562): hold definitions_cache().write() across check -> build -> store (single-flight), with BUILD_COUNT incremented only on the stored build; the read-lock fast path for cache hits stays. Before landing, audit for re-entrancy/deadlock: build_tool_definitions() (:584) calls okf get_global_librarian().try_lock() and mcp_client::tool_definitions() (bridge/block_in_place, :212) — neither takes the definitions_cache write lock, and invalidate_tool_definitions() is never called from build, so holding the write lock across build must not deadlock; if the MCP-bridge-under-write-lock audit finds a real problem, fall back to build-outside + re-check under write lock and discard the loser (count only the stored build). Acceptance: repro test fails pre-fix, passes post-fix; no behavior change to cached content (existing content-equality tests still pass)."
        },
        {
          "id": "294.3",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Lock the unlocked test callers found in 294.1 (test-only change)",
          "details": "Add `let _tl = crate::tools::subagent_tool::test_env_lock();` at the top of every test found in 294.1 that calls tool_definitions()/tool_definitions_excluding() (or a path reaching them) without holding it — at minimum the tools/mod.rs and subagent_tool.rs tests listed in task details. This closes window (b) for future tests too; it is a complement to 294.2, not a substitute (lock discipline already failed once — the production single-flight fix is what makes the count robust). Do not refactor unrelated tests. Acceptance: grep shows zero remaining unlocked tool_definitions() callers in test modules, or each remainder is justified in the PR description."
        },
        {
          "id": "294.4",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Verify: 3x parallel green, single-threaded green, checks at baseline; PR to PreRelese",
          "details": "Run: `cargo test --lib` 3x consecutively (default parallel, all green at re-baselined counts); `cargo test --lib -- --test-threads=1` green; `cargo test --lib tools::` 3x green; `cargo check --lib` zero warnings; `cargo check --tests` baseline-identical (only known 262/273 issues). Prepare a PR against PreRelese (never master, no force-push) with the mechanism, the fix, and the audit list in its description; push/PR only on John's approval per standing Quartermaster rules. Acceptance: all verification runs green and the PR is ready (or merged on his tap)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 295,
      "title": "Helix installer hook: install/update chat-mcp during install (Rust)",
      "description": "John-approved 2026-11-03 (Rust, not script): add a Rust step to Helix installer.rs that installs/updates chat-mcp during a Helix install: binary into ~/.local/bin/chat-mcp built from the micro-tech/chat-mcp repo source, config dir ~/.config/chat-mcp, and the [[mcp.servers]] chat block in Helix config.toml if missing (backup first, never duplicate). Sandbox only: no push, no PR, no deploy, no R630 touch. Token safety is a hard rule: never embed, print, or require a token; preserve an existing chat-mcp config untouched; create a missing one with hub_url and watch_timeout_secs only and no token key, perms 0600. Task 262 interaction: do NOT decide 262.4; the hook is a separate lib module plus a guarded call site and never touches the 262-broken include_str paths.",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [],
      "details": "Live shape proven on the R630 2026-11-03: binary at /home/cobble/.local/bin/chat-mcp, config 0600 at /home/cobble/.config/chat-mcp/config.toml, chat block appended to ~/helix/config.toml with a .bak backup made first, then systemctl restart helix. Hook ordering in install(): after config.toml is deployed (the block edit needs it) and before the service starts (so the first start picks the chat server up). Ownership of the new binary and config dir is the installer call site's job (chown to the runtime user); the lib module only writes files. Uninstall leaves chat-mcp in place, like config and logs.",
      "testStrategy": "All 295.x strategies green; orchestrator three-path test green (fresh install, idempotent re-run, existing-config-preserved); cargo check --lib zero warnings; installer bin compiles with the 262 lines temporarily neutralized (patch reverted, never committed); secret grep clean.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "295.1",
          "title": "Binary sourcing: clone-or-reuse chat-mcp repo, cargo build --release, install to ~/.local/bin",
          "status": "done"
        },
        {
          "id": "295.2",
          "title": "Config dir + file: preserve-if-exists, create-if-missing with hub_url + watch_timeout_secs, no token, 0600",
          "status": "done"
        },
        {
          "id": "295.3",
          "title": "Helix config block: append [[mcp.servers]] chat if missing, backup first, never duplicate header or block",
          "status": "done"
        },
        {
          "id": "295.4",
          "title": "installer.rs call site: guarded warn-not-fail, after config deploy, before service start, plus ownership",
          "status": "done"
        },
        {
          "id": "295.5",
          "title": "Verification: checks, full lib suite counts, secret grep, branch + commit (no junk)",
          "status": "done"
        }
      ]
    },
