      "details": "Order is load-bearing: sender check FIRST, before any parsing or execution. Message sender must be in [chat_command] allowed_senders (expected values \"cobble-jr\", \"john\"; the hub stamps sender from the token name and drops spoofed sender fields — server.rs anti-spoofing comment + store.rs Envelope). Any other sender, including \"helix\" (loop prevention: Helix's own replies never re-trigger), is ignored silently (no reply) and audit-logged at info level. Then trigger: trimmed body must start with \"!\"; otherwise ignored silently (debug log). Strip \"!\", trim; empty remainder replies \"empty command\". Remainder starting with \"asus:\" replies \"ASUS relay is Phase 2 (not enabled yet)\" in Phase 1. Cap: max_commands_per_tick commands per tick; extras wait for the next tick (cursor advances only past processed messages).",
      "testStrategy": "Unit tests: allowed senders execute; helix/grok-cli/other senders ignored (no execution, no reply, audit logged); non-'!' messages ignored; empty command replies an error; 'asus:' in Phase 1 replies not-enabled; cursor advances per message.",
