    {
      "id": 299,
      "title": "Read-only executor (local)",
      "description": "Allowlist + metachar rejection + direct Command execution with no shell, timeout, and audit logging.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
        298
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Parse the command line into argv by whitespace split (NO quoting in v1 — any token containing a quote char is rejected). Reject if: empty argv; any token contains a metacharacter from | > < ; & $ ` \\ \" ' * ? ~ ( ) { } or a newline/control char. argv[0] must be in the hardcoded v1 allowlist (code, NOT config): cat, tail, head, grep, ls, ps, df, free, uptime, whoami, hostname, systemctl — with systemctl restricted: second token must be one of status, is-active, show, list-units (any other subcommand rejected). Execute via std::process::Command directly (NO shell — this is what makes the allowlist airtight; do NOT use run_shell for this path, it allows writes). Timeout = command_timeout_secs (default 30). Capture stdout + stderr (stderr appended under a [stderr] marker if non-empty), truncate to max_output_bytes with a [truncated] note. Non-zero exit: output still posted, prefixed with an [exit N] line. Audit-log EVERY execution via log_to_file: timestamp, sender, target, command, exit code, duration ms, output bytes. The executor takes the allowlist as a parameter (production passes the hardcoded set; tests pass a set including sleep for the timeout test). Optional defense-in-depth: run validate_shell_command (shell_security.rs:204) over the joined string as a second layer, only if it never widens what the allowlist permits.",
      "testStrategy": "Unit tests: each allowlisted command executes; writes rejected (rm, cp, mv, touch, systemctl restart/stop, redirect attempts); metachar rejection (pipe, redirect, semicolon, $(), backtick, quote); systemctl subcommand restriction; timeout test via injected allowlist (sleep past a 1s test timeout, no hang); audit lines present for executions and rejections.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "299.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Argv parse + metachar rejection (no shell)",
          "details": "Whitespace split, no quoting. Reject metachars and control chars in any token. Execute via std::process::Command only."
        },
        {
          "id": "299.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Hardcoded allowlist + systemctl subcommand restriction",
          "details": "Allowlist in code, not config. systemctl limited to status/is-active/show/list-units."
        },
        {
          "id": "299.3",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Timeout, output cap, and audit logging",
          "details": "Timeout from config (default 30s); truncate to max_output_bytes with a note; log every execution and rejection."
        }
      ]
    },
