      "id": 300,
      "title": "Reply chunking + send",
      "description": "Echo the command, split output into 8KB-safe chunks, and post them in order to the same room.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
        299
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Reply format: first line echoes the command ($ <command> for local, asus$ <command> for ASUS in Phase 2), then output. Chunking: split the full reply into <= chunk_bytes (default 7500) BYTE chunks on UTF-8 char boundaries (never split a character), prefix each chunk \"[n/m] \" (chunk budget includes the prefix). Send sequentially via mcp__chat__chat_send to the SAME room (the command room from config), ~150 ms between chunks (hub rate-limit pacing, ~10 msg/s burst), retry once on failure (including 429, after a short sleep), then abandon remaining chunks (logged, not retried forever). Command failure/timeout posts the error text as the reply — never silent. Empty output becomes a single reply \"(no output)\".",
      "testStrategy": "Unit tests: chunking at the byte boundary (exact/under/over); multibyte safety (chunks reassemble to the original); numbering correct; empty output single reply. Integration with stub chat_send: chunks sent in order to the same room; send-failure retry-once then abandon (assert via stub call counts).",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "300.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Byte-safe chunking with [n/m] numbering",
          "details": "7500-byte default budget including prefix; never split a UTF-8 character; chunks reassemble exactly."
        },
        {
          "id": "300.2",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Sequential send with pacing + retry-once",
          "details": "Same room, ~150 ms pacing, retry once on failure/429, then abandon with a log line. Errors always posted, never silent."
        }
      ]
    },
