    {
      "id": 302,
      "title": "Docs + Phase 1 live drill",
      "description": "Document the loop and prove it live on the R630 with positive and negative cases.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [
        301
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Docs file docs/chat-command-loop.md: room name + auto-create note (hub rooms auto-create on first post — no manual step); trigger syntax; exact allowlist + systemctl restriction; sender rule (cobble-jr, john only; helix excluded = loop prevention); fail-closed defaults (empty allowed_senders, routine ships disabled); chunking (7500 B, [n/m]); audit log location; how to enable (set [chat_command] room + allowed_senders in config.toml, then enable the routine via web UI toggle or routines.json); troubleshooting (tools not advertised means quiet skip; routine disabled means nothing; empty allowed_senders means nothing executes); guidance (tail logs, do not cat whole files — 128 KB cap). Live drill (John's steps, on the R630 after deploy): 1) Set config + enable routine. 2) Cobble jr posts !hostname to the command room, Helix replies with the R630 hostname. 3) John posts !whoami, Helix replies. 4) Helix token posts !hostname: IGNORED (no execution, no reply). 5) Cobble jr posts !systemctl restart helix: REJECTED reply, nothing restarted. 6) Long-output command (e.g. !ps aux): chunked replies in order, reassembled equals full output. 7) Cobble jr posts hello (no !): ignored, no reply. Drill passes only if ALL items behave as specified, with audit log lines present for each execution/rejection.",
      "testStrategy": "Drill checklist above, all items verified by John in the room plus audit log lines for each execution/rejection. Docs reviewed for accuracy against the implemented behavior.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
