      "id": 308,
      "title": "Chat-command replies: append [exit N] status line",
      "description": "Helix chat-command replies echo the command and its output but omit the exit status, though the design specified an [exit N] line. Add it.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "Root cause (2026-11-04 drill): the executor captures the exit code (executor.rs exit_code: Option<i32>, set from the process status, tested for 0 and for grep-no-match 1), but the reply builder (reply.rs) never renders it, so the 2026-11-04 !uptime reply carried [1/1] $ uptime plus output and no exit line. Fix: append the exit status after the output and before chunking, so it rides the last chunk: Some(N) renders as [exit N]; None (killed by signal) renders as [exit signal] so the case is visible, not silently dropped. Apply to both the local reply path and the ASUS (!asus:) reply path if they render separately. Do not change the allowlist, the sender gate, or the chunk size.",
      "testStrategy": "Unit tests in the chat_command module: a successful command reply contains [exit 0]; a non-zero command (grep with no match, exit 1) reply contains [exit 1]; a multi-chunk reply carries [exit N] in the last chunk only; a signal-killed command renders [exit signal]. Full cargo test --lib green. Live check after deploy: !uptime in the command room shows [exit 0] in Helix's reply.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "308.1",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Thread exit_code into reply text",
          "details": "Render [exit N] (or [exit signal] for None) after output, before chunking, on local and ASUS reply paths. Add the unit tests above."
        },
        {
          "id": "308.2",
          "status": "pending",
          "title": "Live re-drill: !uptime shows [exit 0]",
          "details": "After deploy, post !uptime in the command room and confirm Helix's reply ends with [exit 0]."
        }
      ]
    },
