      "id": 310,
      "title": "LLM task handler (async, scope-enforced, per-backend queue)",
      "description": "Run llm tasks as agent jobs on the named backend (server, desktop, or gemini), async with ACK plus result or timeout reports, scope-enforced tools, and a per-backend FIFO queue with busy and queued replies.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
        309
      ],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Implement spec section 6: handler takes (task string, backend, time budget, scope). Spawns an agent run on the named backend following the commander pattern (backend as commander, may delegate to sub-agents), using Helix's existing agent-run machinery — do not invent a new LLM client. Async: the accepting tick posts an ACK (accepted, backend, budget) and returns; a later tick or callback posts the RESULT (or a timeout report with partial results if the budget expires). Scope enforcement by tool allowlist at spawn: read removes all write tools (labels, archives, edits, sends, file writes) — a read task attempting a write fails closed and the report says so; write:<domain> allows writes only in that domain. Concurrency: one running task per backend; a task for a busy backend QUEUES FIFO per backend, sender gets a reply stating the backend is running plus queue position; a task for an idle backend runs immediately; no queue cap in v1. Reports: same command room, chunked [n/m], citing the task hub message id, never starting with !; read reports state explicitly that no writes were made (or list writes for write tasks). Audit-log every acceptance, start, completion, timeout, rejection, and busy or queued reply.",
