    {
      "id": 315,
      "title": "Cpu mutex held across whole routines, starving heartbeat",
      "description": "The Cpu mutex is held across whole routine runs, so a long self-improve cycle or nightly fix blocks the heartbeat tick and all other routines for minutes, tripping the missed-beat watchdog.",
      "status": "pending",
      "dependencies": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "details": "Bot review 2026-11-05 (PreRelese 17fddd7), Part B Must-fix 3. Evidence: src/main.rs:401 spawns per-routine_run and holds cpu.lock() across handle_routine_run().await (src/cpu/mod.rs:436); the heartbeat tick takes the same lock (src/main.rs:429). A self-improve cycle (up to max_cycle_minutes of LLM work) or a nightly fix (LLM loop + cargo test --lib, src/cpu/mod.rs:1097) blocks all beats and all other routines for minutes. Also routine_chat_command_watch runs the sync tick() (up to the 45 s TICK_BUDGET) while holding the lock. Fix: do not hold the Cpu lock across routine execution - move the lock inside the short critical sections, or run routines on a dedicated task with the heartbeat on its own state.",
      "testStrategy": "Heartbeat beats continue during a long routine run (no missed-beat watchdog trips); cargo test --lib green.",
      "subtasks": [],
      "results": ""
    },
